[Prop:shadow3 of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Let \(l\) be a component of the frontier of \(\Theta(\widetilde{S})\) in \(P_{\varphi}\). Then,
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(l\) is a slice leaf of \(\mathcal{F}^{s/u}\). If it is a slice leaf \(l\) of \(\mathcal{F}^{s}\), then as a sequence of point \(\{p_{n}\}_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\) tends to a point in \(l\), the preimages \((\Theta|_{\widetilde{S}})^{-1}(p_{n})\) in \(\widetilde{S}\) escape in the positive direction.
Similar conclusion holds for unstable boundary slice leaves.
\item \(l\) is periodic, namely, there is an element \(g\in \pi_{1}(M)\) such that \(g\) fixes \(l\) and hence a unique point in \(l\).
\end{enumerate}

[Lem 7 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Let $\delta\in (0,1/2),\mathsf C>0$, $X\sim \Hyp(n_1,n,m)$ with $\mathbb EX=\frac{n_1m}{n}\leq  \mathsf CN^\delta$. There exists constants $C,c$ depending on $\mathsf C$ such that
            \begin{equation}
                \mathbb P(X\geq 2a)\leq C\exp(-ca) \mbox{ for all } a\geq 3\mathsf CN^q.
            \end{equation}

