[Coro 9 of arXiv:2604.07579, 'Topology of Percolation Clusters: Central Limit Theorems beyond the Lattice'] Assume $\Gamma$ has subexponential growth. Since
    the sequence of metric balls $(B_{r})$ is an exhaustive F{\o}lner
    sequence in any vertex-transitive graph, the conclusions of Theorem \ref{TLC_func}
    apply to $(B_{r})$. Specifically, under the same stabilization and moment
    conditions, we have
    \begin{enumerate}
      \item $\lim_{r\to\infty}|B_{r}|^{-1}\Var_{p}(F(B_{r})) = \sigma^{2}$,
        and

      \item $|B_{r}|^{-1/2}(F(B_{r}) - \E_{p}[F(B_{r})]) \overset{d}{\Longrightarrow}
        \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^{2})$,
    \end{enumerate}
    where $\sigma^{2}$ is the asymptotic variance defined in Theorem
    \ref{TLC_func}.

