[Theorem 11 (Upper bound for the within-path ridge estimator) of arXiv:2608.22179, '\bf Token-Level Likelihood-Array Regression for Membership Inference and AI-Generated Text'] There exists a constant $C<\infty$ such that, for every $0<\lambda\leq1$,
\begin{equation}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_\nu(M)}
\mathbb E_P
\|\widehat{\eta}_\lambda-\eta_0\|_{P_\Phi}^2
\leq
C
\left\{
\lambda
+
\frac{
\lambda^{-1/\nu}\log(e/\lambda)
}{n}
\right\}.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma L: reduced definition of arXiv:2511.11036, 'Analysis of a class of Recursive Distributional Equations Including the Resistance of the '] Let $\mathcal{F} : \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a continuous function that is nondecreasing in the second argument and $Q : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be continuous.  An upper semicontinuous function $F : \mathbb{R} \times (0,+\infty) \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfies $\partial_{t} F - \mathcal{F} ( \partial_{x} F, \partial^{2}_{x} F ) + Q(F) \leq 0$ in the viscosity sense if and only if it has the following property: If $\varphi$ is a smooth test function that touches $F$ from above at some point $(x_{0},t_{0})$ and
		\begin{align*}
			\text{either (i)} \quad \partial_{x} \varphi(x_{0},t_{0}) \neq 0, \quad \text{or (ii)} \quad  \partial_{x} \varphi(x_{0},t_{0}) = \partial_{x}^{2} \varphi(x_{0},t_{0}) = 0,
		\end{align*}
	then 
		\begin{equation*}
			\partial_{t} \varphi(x_{0},t_{0}) \leq \mathcal{F} ( \partial_{x} \varphi(x_{0},t_{0}), \partial_{x}^{2} \varphi(x_{0},t_{0}) ).
		\end{equation*}

[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2609.03793, 'Typical martingale diverges on a co-$\sigma$-porous set'] Let $\alpha>0$ and $r_0>0$ be arbitrary. Let also $F\subset 2^\N$ be such that
\begin{equation}

\forall x\in 2^\N\forall r\in(0,r_0)\exists y\in 2^\N:B_{\rhoexp}(y,\alpha r)\subset B_{\rhoexp}(x,r)\setminus F.
\end{equation}
Then $F$ is measurable and $P(F)=0$.

