    \[
    \btheta_-
    = \hbA_- \hbg_-\,,\quad
    \textup{where}\quad
    \hbA_- = \bigg((\hbD_-)^{-1} - \frac{m(z_\star)}{\alpha}\bI_{B_-}\bigg)^{-1}\,.
    \]
Recall that $\hbD_-$ is a diagonal matrix with (negative) diagonal entries $\hv_j$. It follows that $\hbA_-$ is a diagonal matrix with (negative) diagonal entries
    \[\bigg(
    \frac{1}{\hv_j}-\frac{m(z_\star)}{\alpha}\bigg)^{-1}
    = \frac{\alpha\hv_j}{\alpha-\hv_j m(z_\star)} \ge \hv_j\,,
    \]
