[Prop second_moment_critical_dim_asymptotics of arXiv:2508.18809, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation III: The upper critical dimension}'] If $d=3\alpha<6$ then there exists a positive constant $A$ such that
\begin{equation}

  \mathbb E_{\beta_c,r}|K|^2 \sim \frac{\alpha}{\beta_c}\frac{A r^{3\alpha}}{\sqrt{\log r}}.
