body:
[Lemma 13 (Bulk truncation of the Palm projection) of arXiv:2608.20101, '\bfseries Largest bulk gap of the complex Ginibre ensemble'] Fix \(s<1\) and \(C_0<\infty\).  There exist \(c,C>0\) such that, uniformly
for \(|a|\le s\), \(0\le r\le C_0n^{-1/2}(\log n)^{1/4}\), and
\(w\in D_r(a)\),
\begin{align}
 0&\le K_{\infty,n}^a(w,w)-K_n^a(w,w)\le Cne^{-cn},
 \\
 0&\le K_{\infty,n}(a,a)-K_n(a,a)\le Cne^{-cn}.

\end{align}
Consequently, for \(D=D_r(a)\),
\begin{equation}
 \Tr\!\left[\one_D(K_{\infty,n}^a-K_n^a)\one_D\right]
 \le Cnr^2e^{-cn}.
\end{equation}

[Corollary cor.dpi of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Fix $p > 4$ and $(t_0,m_0) \in [0,1) \times \mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R})$. Let $(m,\alpha) \in \mathcal{A}(t_0,m_0)$ be such that
    \begin{equation*}
        |\alpha(t,x)| \leq C,\qquad\text{for a.e.\ } (t,x)\in[t_0,t_0+1]\times{\mathbb R},
    \end{equation*}
    where $C>0$ is an arbitrary constant. Then, for any $h\in(0,1-t_0)$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{V}_p^+(t_0,m_0) \leq \mathcal{V}_p^+\big( t_0 + h, m_{t_0 + h} \big).
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

