body:
[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Let $K$ be a weakly inhomogeneous random graph, with associated edge probabilities $(p_e)_{e \in E}$. Then, for any sequence $\lambda_n \to +\infty$ with $\lambda_n \leq n$,
    \begin{equation}
        \#\{e \in K: p_e \geq \frac{\lambda_n}{n} \} = o_\Proba(n).
    \end{equation}

    In particular, there exists $\overline{K} \sim \mc{G}(n, \frac{\lambda_n}{n})$ such that $K \lesssim_{n \to +\infty} \overline{K}$.

