[Lemma lem:finite-part-uniqueness-comp of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Assume $h_{\rm rem}\in H^{\frac12}(\partial\Omega)$. Then (equation eq:finite-part-variational-comp of the paper) has a unique solution \(v^{\rm reg}\in H^1(\Omega)\), and
\begin{align}
 \nm{v^{\rm reg}}_{H^1(\Omega)}
 \le
 C\left(
 \nm{h_{\rm rem}}_{H^{\frac12}(\partial\Omega)}
 +
 \nm{f^{\rm cut}}_{H^{-1}(\Omega)}
 \right).

\end{align}
Therefore the normalized singular solution \(u=H^{\rm sing}+v^{\rm reg}\) exists, is independent of the radial cutoffs, and is unique among functions with the prescribed singular germs and an \(H^1\) regular correction.

