[Proposition prop_1 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] For $0< b<1$  and integer $m\geq1$ define the sequence of functions  

  \begin{eqnarray}

\theta_m(b)=-\frac{1}{b^{m+1}}\Big(\ln(1-b)+b+\frac{b^2}{2}+\frac{b^3}{3}+\cdots+\frac{b^m}{m}\Big).
\end{eqnarray}  
If $A$ is symmetric, then HWI holds with 
\begin{eqnarray}

\kappa=\frac{b^*}{4}\approx 0.1457, 
\end{eqnarray}
 where $b^*$ is the unique solution for $b$ in the equation\footnote{The equation $2b\theta_1(b)=1$ simplifies to $\ln(1-b)=-\frac{3}{2}b$.  } $2b\theta_1(b)=1$.

[Lemma 20 (Pointwise comparison-image lower bound) of arXiv:2608.30722, 'Intermediate Singular Values of Random Matrices\\ under Second-Moment and Anti-Concentrati'] For every deterministic choice of \(S\subseteq[m_l]\) with \(|S|=l\) and every
fixed \(y\in S^{l-1}\),
\begin{equation}
  \bbP\!\left(
    \|B_S X_S(y)\|_2 \le c_\ast\sqrt{\frac{n}{l}}
    \ \text{ and }\ 
    \cE_2^c
  \right)
  \;\le\;
  e^{-c_{\mathrm{sb}} l}.
\end{equation}

