{"artifact_digest":"sha256:fd112b51fa93c21eacd71294823cb3b7169ace760784d6bf505dbcd59b9098ba","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/fd/fd112b51fa93c21eacd71294823cb3b7169ace760784d6bf505dbcd59b9098ba.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:7ed7820dced0fd15b99103b59bf8c9aac894ce17b85f6bd808c7ab0e951eaa2a","bundle_entry_key":"2608-26765-lemma-18-local-second-moment-expansion","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_117","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_117.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-26765-lemma-18-local-second-moment-expansion","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Unroll Equation~(equation eq:E1 of the paper) for $h$ steps and write the exact decomposition
\begin{equation}

  \theta_{c,h}=x+D_{c,h}+R_{c,h},
\end{equation}
where
\[
  D_{c,h}:=-\gamma\left(h\xi_c+\sum_{j=1}^h\varepsilon_{c,j}\right),
  \qquad
  R_{c,h}:=-\gamma\sum_{\ell=0}^{h-1}f'(\theta_{c,\ell}).
\]
Expanding the square gives
\begin{equation}

