[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2606.31936, 'Coupling and Maximal Inequalities for Graph-Dependent Empirical Processes'] For any $\mathcal B \subseteq \mathcal F$, and partition $\mathcal P_{M}$ and any associated proper $(r,K)$-coloring $\mathcal C_{r,K}$ the following statements are true 
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $\boldsymbol{\tau}_{\mathcal B , G_{n}} \leq  ||f||_{\infty} \boldsymbol{\tau}_{\operatorname{cone} \mathcal B , G_{n}}$, for any $r,q \in \mathbb{N}$. 
		\item $q \mapsto \tau_{  \mathcal B , G_{n}}(r,q)$ is non-decreasing.
		\item $\mathcal B \mapsto \boldsymbol{\tau}_{\mathcal B , G_{n}}$ is non-decreasing (under the inclusion ordering).
	\end{enumerate}

