[Theorem disth of arXiv:2606.15203, 'The existence of invariant sublinear expectations for $G\text{-}$SDEs'] If Assumption (Ass1 of the paper) and (Ass2 of the paper) hold, then there exists $T_{\infty} \in \mathcal{M}$, such that
 \begin{equation}
   \rho_{\beta}((\bar{T}^{k})^*T_{\delta_x},T_{\infty})\rightarrow 0\ \ as\ k\rightarrow \infty,
 \end{equation}
where $T_{\delta_x}\varphi=\varphi(x)$ for any $x \in \mathbb{R}^d$, $\varphi \in B_b(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $(\bar{T}^k)^{*}T_{\delta_x}=T_{\delta_x}\bar{T}^k$.

