[Lemma lem: upsilon2 of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] Let $\mathbb P^0$ be a law on admissible boundary conditions $\varphi^0:=(W^0,Z^0)$. Then for every $\alpha \in (0,1)$, there exists $C>0$ such that, for every $T>0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E_{\mathbb P^0\otimes \mathbb P^0} [|\Upsilon_{2,T}(W^0_-+Z^0_-,W^0_++Z^0_+)|^\alpha]\leq C + \mathbb E_{\mathbb P^0\otimes \mathbb P^0}[\|Z^0_+\|_{H^{1/2-\kappa}_z}^2+\|Z^0_-\|_{H^{1/2-\kappa}_z}^2]. 
\end{equation}
Furthermore, the pushforward under the regularized boundary measure $(\Upsilon_{2, T})^* (\nu^0_T\otimes \nu^0_T)$ converges in law to a random variable 
  $(\Upsilon_{2,\infty})^* (\nu^0\otimes \nu^0)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:RBJ-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The one-point Fredholm determinant
$F_{t, a, n} = \det(I - K_{t, a, n})$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
p F_{t, a, n+1} F_{t+1, a+2, n}
+ q F_{t+1, a+1, n} F_{t, a+1, n+1}
- F_{t, a+1, n} F_{t+1, a+1, n+1}
= 0,
\end{equation}
at every $(t, a, n)$ with $a < y_{n+1} + t - 1$.

[Lemma lem:truncation of arXiv:2608.09368, 'A proof of Ross's conjecture for two-site moving-target search'] For every $n\ge1$,
\begin{equation}
 0\le V(p)-V_n(p)
 \le\frac{V_{\mathrm{ref}}^2}{nC_{\min}}
 \qquad\text{for all }p\in[0,1].

\end{equation}
Consequently $V_n\to V$ uniformly.

[Lemma L:M-lemma of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] For $\mathcal{M}^\rho$ from Definition (D:prelandscapes of the paper), it has a continuous extension to $\mathbb H^2_\uparrow$, and this extension satisfies parts $1, 2, 4, 5, 6$, and $7$ of Proposition (P:properties-elpp of the paper) (in the place of $\mathcal{Q}^\rho$ there).    
        Moreover, for any $q > 0, c \in \mathbb{R}$ if we consider the rescaling
        \begin{equation}

            \mathcal{M}^{\rho, q, c}(x, s; y, t) := q^{-1} \mathcal{M}^\rho(q^2 x, q^3 s + c; q^2 y, q^3 t + c)
        \end{equation}
        then $\mathcal{M}^{\rho, q, c}|_{\mathbb{Q}^4 \cap \mathbb H^2_\uparrow}$ is a half-space pre-landscape of parameter $q \alpha$.

[Lemma lem: H-1 estimate_local_nonlinear of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] Let $\omega$ be the global solution provided by (prop:global_well_cutoff of the paper) and $T>0$. For every $p\ge1$ there exists a constant $K(T, \nu, p)$ such that it holds
