body:
[Definition Radon measure of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] A (real) \emph{Radon measure} \(\mu\) on \(\mathbb{R}^d\) is a countably additive set function
\[
  \mu: \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^d) \;\longrightarrow\; \mathbb{R}
\]
satisfying the following two regularity properties:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Local finiteness.} For every compact set \(K \subset \mathbb{R}^d\), one has \(\lvert \mu\rvert(K) < \infty\).
  \item \textbf{Regularity.}
  \begin{itemize}
    \item \emph{Inner regularity:} For every Borel set \(E \subset \mathbb{R}^d\),
    \[
      \mu(E) \;=\; \sup\,\{\,\mu(K)\colon K \subset E,\; K \text{ compact}\}.
    \]
    \item \emph{Outer regularity:} For every Borel set \(E \subset \mathbb{R}^d\),
    \[
      \mu(E) \;=\; \inf\,\{\,\mu(U)\colon U \supset E,\; U \text{ open}\}.
    \]
  \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}

