[Proposition 10 (Half-bridge correction) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] The updates
\begin{equation}
f_0^{(n+1)}=(\mathsf Kg_T^{(n)})^{-1},
\qquad
g_T^{(n+1)}=(\mathsf K^*f_0^{(n+1)})^{-1}
\end{equation}
are alternating KL projections onto the two marginal constraint sets and converge in Hilbert's projective metric to \((f_0,g_T)\), up to reciprocal gauge. The first factor is the source corrector omitted by a terminal-only construction. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:basic-facts-probability of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ be a gamble space, and let $A\subseteq\Omega$.
  Then
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item $\underline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A = 1 - \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A^c$.
  \end{enumerate}
  If gambles are furthermore arbitrage-free and positive-linear, then
  \begin{enumerate}[resume]
  \item $0 \leq \underline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A \leq \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A \leq 1$.
  \item $\overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A + \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A^c \geq 1$.
  \end{enumerate}

