[Prop of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Fix $\beta \in (0,1)$ and let $H_n(\beta)$ be the height of the tree $T_n$. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{H_n(\beta)}{n^{1-\beta}}\stackrel{P}{\longrightarrow} \frac{2}{1-\beta}.
    \end{align*}

