[Lemma eq:Tlm-k of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] For $i\neq j, q\in \{1,2\}$, under the Palm probability measure of mixed handovers of type $\bbinom{q}{i,j}$, the Laplace transform of $T$ is

\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}^0_{{\mathcal W }_{i,j}^{(q)}}\left[e^{-\rho T}\right]=\frac{4\lambda_1\lambda_2 v_1v_2}{L^{(q)}_{i,j}} \, \xi_{i,j}^{q}(\rho,v_i,v_j), 

\end{equation}

where the functions $\xi_{i,j}^{(q)}(\rho,v_i,v_j)$ are determined in ((eq:T12j of the paper)), ((eq:T12m of the paper)), ((eq:T121g of the paper)) and ((eq:T1225 of the paper)), respectively, for the four different cases for  $i\neq j, q\in \{1,2\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop Prop_UniformFredholmMapsAreStableUnderTransverseBaseChange of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Let ${\mathbf{X}}$, ${\mathbf{Y}}$, and ${\mathbf{Z}}$ be tame Fréchet manifolds,
  $f \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace {\mathbf{X}} \to {\mathbf{Y}}$ uniformly Fredholm and
  $g \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace {\mathbf{Z}} \to {\mathbf{Y}}$ tame smooth.
  If $f$ and $g$ are \defined{transverse};
  that is: for every $(x,z) \in {\mathbf{X}} \times {\mathbf{Z}}$ with $f(x) = g(z) \eqcolon y$
  the map $T_xf + T_zg \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace T_x{\mathbf{X}} \oplus T_z{\mathbf{Z}} \to T_y{\mathbf{Y}}$ is surjective;
  then:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item
    the fibre product
    \begin{equation*}
      g^*{\mathbf{X}} \coloneq \set[\big]{ (x,z) \in {\mathbf{X}} \times {\mathbf{Z}} : f(x) = g(z) }
    \end{equation*}
    is a tame Fréchet submanifold, and
  \item
    the map $g^*f \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace g^*{\mathbf{X}} \to {\mathbf{Z}}$ is uniformly Fredholm and $\ind g^*f = \paren{\ind f} \circ f^*g$.
  \end{enumerate}

