body:
[Prop equiv represent of bP^h of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Assume that $h$ satisfies the mean-value property (equation Equation:MeanValueProperty of the paper). Let $\mathbf{P}^h$ be as defined in (equation Definition:h-transform,general case with r0 of the paper). Then,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{P}^h=\frac{\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{ \tau^0>T \right\}}}{r_0}\frac{h(T,X_T)}{h(0,X_0)}\mathbf{P}.
\end{equation}
In other words, $\mathbf{P}^h$ is supported on $\left\{ \tau^0>T \right\}$, where $(t,X_t)\in\mathcal A_h$ for all $t\in[0,T]$.

