[Proposition 15 (Gaussian-rate super-Poincar\'e inequality) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There are $A_{\gamma,Q},B_{\gamma,Q}<\infty$ such that, for all $s>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\C} f^2\,\D\nu
 \le s\int_{\C}|\nabla f|^2\,\D\nu
 +A_{\gamma,Q}e^{B_{\gamma,Q}/s}\left(\int_{\C}|f|\,\D\nu\right)^2.
\end{equation}

