[Definition 48 of arXiv:2603.28734, 'Free energy analyticity of the disordered XY model and Debye screening in the 2D Coulomb g'] Fix a subgraph $G$ of $\Z^d$, a configuration $\tau \in \Pi_G$, and $-\infty \leq -t < -s \leq 0$. 
\begin{itemize}
\item The $\om$ (resp. $\eta$)-marginal of $R^{\Lambda, -t, -s}(\tau)$ will be denoted by $R_\om^{\Lambda, -t, -s}(\tau)$ (resp. $R_\eta^{\Lambda, -t, -s}(\tau)$). 
\item The $(\om,\eta)$-marginal of $R^{\Lambda, -t, -s}(\tau)$ will be denoted by $R_{(\om,\tau)}^{\Lambda, -t, -s}(\tau)$.
\item The $\alpha$-marginal of $R^{\Lambda, -t, -s}(\tau)$ will be denoted by $R_\alpha^{\Lambda, -t, -s}(\tau)$. 
