body:
[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2608.13358, 'Extreme points of sets of probability measures and $\phi$-divergences'] Let $\Omega_1,\ldots, \Omega_n$ be finite sets, each carrying its power set as a $\sigma$-algebra.\ Moreover, let $\cM:=\Pi(p_1,\ldots,p_n)$ be the set of multi-marginal couplings of $p_1,\ldots,p_n$, let $q\in \cM$ with $p'\ll q$ for all $p'\in \cM$, and let $\varphi\colon[0,\infty)\to\R$ be a convex function satisfying $\varphi(1)=0$ and $\varphi_+'(0)=-\infty$.\ Then, for $p\in\cM$, the following statements are equivalent.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $p$ is an extreme point of $\cM$.
        \item $p$ is a strict local maximizer of the function
        \begin{equation}
            \cM \to \R,\quad p' \mapsto \Div{\varphi}{p'}{q}.
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

