[Definition e.Stratification of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] We say that ${\mathbb G}$ is a \emph{Carnot group} of step $k$ if ${\mathbb G}$  is a connected and simply connected Lie group whose Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}$ is \emph{stratified}, that is, there are non-trivial linear subspaces $V_1,\ldots, V_k$ of $\mathfrak{g}$ such that
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{g}=V_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus V_{k},
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align}
& \left[V_{1}, V_{i-1}\right]=V_{i},\hskip0.1in  V_{i} \neq \{0\}, \hskip0.1in 2 \leqslant i \leqslant k,
\notag
\\
& [ V_{1}, V_{k} ]=\left\{ 0 \right\}.
\end{align}

[Lemma lmm:taylor-derivative of arXiv:2607.02013, 'Resolution of the Detection Threshold Conjecture for Random Geometric Graphs in the $d>n$ '] Fix $r\ge2$ and $N\ge1$.  There exist constants $c_0,c,C>0$, depending
only on $r$ and $N$, such that the following holds.  If $1 \leq a^2 \leq d/4$,

then
\begin{equation}

\int_{U(t)\le c_0/\delta}
\bigg\{ \prod_{i=1}^r |K(t_i)|\bigg\}
\sup_{0\le\theta\le1}
\bigg|
\frac{\partial^N}{\partial\theta^N}L_\theta(t)
\bigg|
\nu^{\otimes r}(\mathrm d t)
\le
C p^r (a^2\delta)^N \,.
\end{equation}

