[Definition 4 of arXiv:2605.31344, 'Subcritical sharpness for real-valued spin models'] Let $\beta$ and $\rho$ be fixed.
    An infinite-volume Gibbs measure is a probability measure $\nu$ on $\mathbb{R}^{V}$, with the $\sigma-$algebra generated by Borel events depending on finitely many vertices, such that for any finite $\Lambda \subset V$ and any bounded measurable function $g: \mathbb{R}^{\Lambda} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, the DLR equation holds:
    \begin{equation*}
        \nu[g] = \int_{\eta \in \mathbb{R}^{V}} \langle g\rangle _{\Lambda, \beta, \rho}^{\eta} \mathrm{d} \nu(\eta).
    \end{equation*}

