[Thm See Theorem~\ref{thm:critical_gauge_scaling_limit} of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix a $d$-dimensional lattice $\Lambda$ and $R\subset \mathbb{R}^d$ as before. Suppose that $H$ is $C^1$ and solves the gauge PDE: $\text{div}(\nabla F(\nabla H))=0$, and that $g_n$ is the critical gauge function on black vertices of $R_n$ with limiting multiplicity $1$ everywhere on $R_n$. Further suppose that
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{u\in B\cap\partial R_n} |(1/n) \log g_n(u) - H(u)| = O(1/n).
    \end{align*}
    We equate $(1/n) \log g_n$ defined on $B\cap R_n$ with its linear interpolation to a continuous function. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{n\to \infty} (1/n) \log g_n 
    \end{align*}
    exists in the topology induced by the supremum norm on continuous functions and is equal to $H$. Similarly, $\lim_{n\to \infty} (1/n) \log f_n = -H.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Retain the setting of Theorem \ref{thm:compact-manifold}. Fix $\mu,\nu \in \cP_2(M)$ satisfying Assumption \ref{assumption}. Let $P^{T}$ denote the $\Schro$ bridge from $\mu$ to $\nu$ computed with reference $R^{T}$, and let $Q^{T}$ denote the path measure defined in \eqref{eq:semigrp-sb-approx}. It holds that
    \begin{align}
        \limsup\limits_{T \to +\infty} \exp(\lambda_1 T)\left(H(Q^{T}|P^{T})+H(P^{T}|Q^{T})\right) < +\infty.
    \end{align}

