Assume that $f$ follows a Besov prior with parameters $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\theta,k)$ and template random variable $X$ with 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{cases} \:\exists\: \eps>0:\,\mathds{E}\bigl[\left\lvertX\right\rvert^{p(1+\eps)}\bigr]< \infty&\text{if }p\in (0,\infty),\\
\:\exists\:  R>0:\, \left\lvertX\right\rvert\stackrel{a.s.}{\leq}R&\text{if }p=\infty.\end{cases}
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
\mathds{P}(X\neq 0)>0.
\end{equation*}
If $f \in B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)$ almost surely and if Properties B and B' are satisfied, then also Property A is satisfied.

