[Lemma lem:JordanUpperBound of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For the Jordan ordering $\widehat{\sigma}_J$, there exists a positive constant $C$ such that for any $n\ge 1$, any vertex $v\in[n]$, and any $S\ge 1$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P} \left( \widehat{\sigma}_{J}(v)\geq S v \right) \leq \frac{C}{S}.
    \end{equation}

