[Lemma lem:product of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] If $z,w\in L_A$ are linearly independent, then
\begin{equation}
 d\leq \rho(z)\rho(w).
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every integer $h\geq1$, if $d>h^2$, the $h$-active
relations span a space of rank at most one.

