[Theorem thm:TLCF_C of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] Let $h\colon S^m\to\mathbb R$ be a symmetric kernel, where $\pr{S,\mathcal{S}}$ is a measurable space, let $\left(X_i\right)_{i\geqslant 1}$ be a strictly stationary sequence. Let $h_1\colon S\to \mathbb R$ be defined  in 
(equation eq:definition_de_h1 of the paper).

Suppose that  conditions (equation eq:TLC_DMR of the paper), (equation eq:condition_sur_beta of the paper) are satisfied, and that  
\begin{equation}
 \exists a>1/2\mbox{ such that }   \max_{k\in \llbracket 1,m\rrbracket}\sup_{\bm{i}\in\operatorname{Inc}^ k}\E{H_{\bm{i},k}^2\pr{\log\pr{1+\abs{H_{\bm{i},k}}} }^a }<+\infty. 
\end{equation}
 Then the following convergence in distribution takes place: 
 \begin{equation}
    \pr{ \frac{\sqrt{n}}{\binom nm}\pr{W_{m,n}\left(h,t\right)-\E{W_{m,n}\left(h,t\right)} } }_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}
     \to \pr{m\sigma t^{m-1}B_t}_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}\mbox{in }C[0,1],
 \end{equation}
 where $\left(B_t\right)_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}$ is a standard Brownian motion and $\sigma^2$ 
 is given by (equation eq:definition_de_sigma of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

