[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] Let \(A \subset \{1,\ldots,n\}\) and choose arbitrary \(\epsilon > 0\). Then, for some \(C_{t,\epsilon}, c_\epsilon > 0\), independent of \(n\), we have
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{\sigma \in \{-1,1\}^{A}}\E\Big|\sum_{j=1}^n \left[\sum_{l=1}^{n} m_{jl}^{(A)}\right] \delta_i m_j^{[A]}(t)\Big|^{2+\ep}\le C_{t,\ep}
    \end{align*}
for all \(i\in A\) and \(0 \le t < c_\epsilon\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 259 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] In the situation of Theorem~\ref{thm:spcurvenonbip}, define the even Green function as $\textnormal{Gr}^+(p_1,p_2) = \textnormal{Gr}(p_1,p_2) + \textnormal{Gr}(p_1,\overline{\varsigma}(p_2))$, where $\textnormal{Gr}$ is the usual Green function on $\Sigma_{\boldsymbol{v}}^{\textnormal{half}}$ with Dirichlet boundary conditions. We have
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\textnormal{Gr}^{+}(p_1,p_2) & = - \frac{1}{4\pi}\left(\textnormal{gr}_{\boldsymbol{v}}(p_1,p_2) + 2\log\bigg|\frac{z_1 - z_2}{z_1 - z_2^*}\bigg| \right)
\end{split}
\end{equation}

