[Lemma lem:semicontinuity of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $(R,b)$ as above. The function $I:\text{AF}(\Lambda,R,b)\to [0,\infty)$ given by 
    \begin{align*}
        I(\omega) = C_b+\int_R \sigma(\omega(x))\, \mathrm{d} x
    \end{align*}
is a good rate function, i.e. it is lower semicontinuous in the weak topology on flows and the level sets $\{\omega\in \text{AF}(\Lambda,R,b):I(\omega)\leq c\}$ are compact. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

