[Theo full_dist-D of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] Consider some masses $m_0,\cdots,m_{k-1}$, non-negative multiple of $1/n$, such that $W(m[k])<1$.
	For any $b \in\{1,\cdots,k\}$, any partition $(J_0,\cdots,J_{b-1})$ of the set $\{0,\cdots,k-1\}$ with non-empty parts, any sequence $(a_0,a_1,\cdots,a_{b-1})$ in ${\cal C}_n^b$ such that the $a_0,a_1,\cdots,a_{b-1}$ are cyclically ordered around ${\cal C}_n$ (i.e. such that turning around the circle we get $a_0\preceq 0\preceq a_1\preceq \cdots \preceq a_{b-1}\preceq a_0 \preceq 0 \cdots$) and such that
	\[ \Leb\left(\fleche{[a_i,a_{i+1 {~\sf mod~} b}]}\right)> W(m(J_i))~~\textrm{ for }i\in\{0,\cdots,b-1\}.\]
	For a valid DDM\xspace,  we have
	\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{P}\left( \bA{k}_j= a_j, \bI{k}_j =J_j,0\leq j \leq b-1\right)=  \prod_{j=0}^{b-1} \frac{Q^{(n)}(m(J_j))}n.
	\end{equation}
	Moreover, if we consider some non-negative masses $M_0,\cdots,M_{b-1}$,
	\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{P}\left( \bA{k}_j = a_j,  \left|\textbf{O}^{(k)}_j\right|=M_j, 0\leq j \leq b-1\right)= \sum_{(J_0,\cdots,J_{b-1}) \in P(k,b)} \prod_{j=0}^{b-1} \frac{Q^{(n)}(m(J_j))}n \mathds{1}_{W(m(J_j)) = M_j}
	\end{equation}
	where, as in Theorem (theo:dqgsrt of the paper), $P(k,b)$ is the set of partitions of $\{0,\ldots, k-1\}$ into $b$ parts. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

