body:
[Prop torus-heights of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] Let $\theta_{n,j} = \frac{(2j+1)\pi}{2n+1}$, and $r=r_{n,j} = 2\cos\theta_{n,j}-2$ be a real root of $P_n$. Then we have
\begin{equation*}
	\rho_r(l_{1,n}^{tor}) = A_r = \begin{pmatrix}1&0 \\r&1\end{pmatrix} \ \ \ \ \ \rho_r(l_{2,n}^{tor}) = -B_r^{4n+2} = -\begin{pmatrix}1&4n+2\\0&1\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation*}
In particular, the central signs are $(+1, -1)$, and the transverse parameters are $(r, 4n+2)$. Let $\widetilde\rho_{n,j}: Q_n^{tor} \to \widetilde{PSL}_2(\mathbb R)$ be the meridian-normalized lift of $\bar\rho_r$, and put $\widetilde\rho_{n,j} = \widetilde{\bar\rho}_{n,j} \circ q_n$. Then
\begin{equation*}
	\mathrm{trans}(\widetilde\rho_{n,j}(l_{1,n}^{tor})) = 0 \ \ \ \ \ \mathrm{trans}(\widetilde\rho_{n,j}(l_{2,n}^{tor})) = 2j+1
\end{equation*}

