body:
[Theorem 14 (Uniform centered dyadic block) of arXiv:2606.26065, 'Localized Centered Second-Chaos Operators'] Assume~\eqref{eq:m-size}, \eqref{eq:S-size}, and Assumption~\ref{ass:time}.  For every finite $p\ge2$ and every $\eps>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{\Lambda\in\Dyd\cup\{\infty\}}
 \left\|\,
 \norm{B^{\circ}_{\Lambda,N,Q,M}}_{C(\Delta_T;\cL(L^2_q,L^2_n))}
 \right\|_{L^p(\Omega)}
 \lesssim_{p,T,\eps}
 C_m C_S^2 C_k\mathcal G(N)
 N^{d/2+\eps}
 \bigl(Q^{d/2+\eps}+M^{d/2+\eps}\bigr).
\end{equation}
Under the Galerkin-state condition in Assumption~\ref{ass:time}, the same estimate holds with the supremum over $\Lambda$ inside the $L^p$ norm, with a constant depending additionally on the uniform finite-state bound $L_{\rm cut}$.  For each fixed dyadic triple,
\begin{equation}
 B^{\circ}_{\Lambda,N,Q,M}
 \longrightarrow B^{\circ}_{\infty,N,Q,M}
 \quad\text{in }L^p\bigl(\Omega;C(\Delta_T;\cL(L^2_q,L^2_n))\bigr).
\end{equation}

