body:
[Lemma 2DHD-lem5.1 of arXiv:2604.21591, '\bf Long-time dynamics of stochastic 2D hydrodynamic-type evolution equations driven by mu'] Assume that $u_0 \in L^2(\Omega,\mathscr{F}_0;H)$ and that Hypotheses $(2DHD-Ass2.0 of the paper)$, $(2DHD-Ass2.1 of the paper)$, and $(2DHD-Ass2.4 of the paper)$ hold. Then, there exists $
	\varepsilon_0=\sqrt{\frac{\mu \lambda_1}{2L_g}}$ such that for any $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2 \in (0,\varepsilon_0]$, $t\geq 0$ and $\kappa \in (0,\frac{\mu\lambda_1}{2})$, the solution $u(t,0,u_0)$ of system  (equation 2DHD-1.01 of the paper) with initial value $u(0)=u_{0}$ satisfies
	\begin{align}
		\mathbb{E}\left[{\left\| {u(t,0,{u_0})} \right\|_{H}^2} \right]+\int_0^t e^{-\kappa (t-s)} {\mathbb{E}\left[ {\left\| {u(s,0,{u_0})} \right\|_{V}^2} \right]ds}\leq e^{-\kappa t}\mathbb{E}\left[\|u_0\|_{H}^2\right] + \rho_1 t,
	\end{align}
	and
	\begin{align}
		\int_0^t {\mathbb{E}\left[ {\left\| {u(s,0,{u_0})} \right\|_{V}^2} \right]ds}  \leq \mathbb{E}\left[\|u_0\|_{H}^2\right] + \rho_1 t,
	\end{align}

	where $\rho_1= \frac{2\kappa+2}{\kappa\min\{2,\mu\}}\left(\frac{2}{\mu}\|f\|_{V'}^2+\frac{\mu\lambda_1}{2}\right)
	$ is a positive constant independent of $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$.

