[Corollary 2603271652 of arXiv:2609.02626, 'Comparison principles and symmetry for subquadratic fractional $p$-Laplacian equations'] Let $N\ge 1$, $s\in (0, \frac12)$, $\frac{1}{1-s}<p< 2$, and $\Omega=B_R$, a Euclidean ball centered at the origin. Suppose that $f\in C_{loc}^{0, 1}(\mathbb R)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
|f(u)|\le C\left(1+|u|^{\frac{Np}{N-sp}-1}\right).
\end{equation}
If $u\in W_0^{s,p}(B_R)$ is a nontrivial non-negative weak solution of (equation main of the paper), then  $u$ is positive in $B_R$, radially symmetric and strictly decreasing with respect to the radius. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:volumes of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\mathbb G=\mathbb H_X\mathbb K_X$ be the decomposition from
Definition~(def:oriented_cone_horiz of the paper). Then
\begin{align}
\operatorname{Vol}(\mathcal C_e^+(\beta,\rho;X))
=
\frac{\beta^{Q-1}\rho^Q}{Q\alpha_X}
\nu_X\bigl(\mathbb B(e,1)\cap\mathbb H_X\bigr).
\end{align}
Moreover, for every $c>0$,
\begin{align}
\int_{\mathcal C_e^+(\beta,\rho;X)}
e^{-c\|g\|^2}\,dg
\geqslant
\frac{\beta^{Q-1}}{\alpha_X}
\nu_X\bigl(\mathbb B(e,1)\cap\mathbb H_X\bigr)
\int_0^\rho
r^{Q-1}e^{-c(1+\beta)^2r^2}\,dr.
\end{align}

