\begin{equation} 
E^n_{\mathsf U (I)}(t):=\begin{cases} 
\frac{1}{|I|}E^n_{I}
, &\text{ if $|I|\neq 0$}
\\
E^n_{\ell}
, &\text{ if $I=\{\ell\}$}.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
for all $I$ bounded intervals. (The choice of notation is because $\mathsf U (I)$ also denotes the uniform probability measure on $I$.)

