[Lem integralordering2 of arXiv:2508.04954, 'Conditional exponential directed last passage percolation under a one-point upper large de'] Let $\mathbf{n} \in {\mathbb N}^3$ and ${\boldsymbol \tau} = 3^{n_{31}}2^{n_{21}}1^{n_{1}}2^{n_{22}}3^{n_{32}}$, where $n_{21}+n_{22}=n_2$ and $n_{31}+n_{32}=n_3$. 
Then, for every ${\boldsymbol \sigma} \in \mathcal S_{\mb{n}}$, 
\begin{equation*}
    \mathrm I^{{\boldsymbol \sigma}}_{{\boldsymbol \tau}} 
    =  \sum_{i=0}^{n_1 \wedge n_{22}} 
    \sum_{j=0}^{ n_{31} \wedge (n_2-i)} (-1)^{\#}
    \mathsf{A}^{n_{1}, n_{22}}_i \mathsf{A}^{n_2-i,n_{31}}_{j}
    \, \mathrm I^{{\boldsymbol \sigma}}_{{\boldsymbol \tau}_{ij}}
\end{equation*}
for some $\#\in {\mathbb Z}$, where ${\boldsymbol \tau}_{ij} = 2^{n_{2}-i-j}(23)^{j}3^{n_{31}-j}(12)^{i}1^{n_{1}-i}3^{n_{32}}$.

