{"artifact_digest":"sha256:43071e0f22e518ec519d3fbc38134651f6f89285643a3aa875a26a223d464261","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/43/43071e0f22e518ec519d3fbc38134651f6f89285643a3aa875a26a223d464261.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:ea870c25942e6d004ffde841200a27cb28ff2de137b3117f3f80d9cec8a29366","bundle_entry_key":"2606-27073-theorem-22-convexity-gap-identity","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_036","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_036.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-27073-theorem-22-convexity-gap-identity","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: For any $x\in S$, the difference of KL divergences with different second arguments is:
\begin{align*}
  \Delta(\mu)
  &= \sum_x\mu(x)\Bigl[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P(x,\cdot)\|\pi) - D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P(x,\cdot)\|\mu P)\Bigr] \\
  &\quad + \sum_x\mu(x)D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P(x,\cdot)\|\mu P) - D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu P\|\pi).
\end{align*}

The first sum equals
\begin{align*}
  \sum_x\mu(x)\sum_y P(x,y)\log\frac{(\mu P)(y)}{\pi(y)}
  &= \sum_y(\mu P)(y)\log\frac{(\mu P)(y)}{\pi(y)} \\
  &= D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu P\|\pi).
\end{align*}

Substituting:
