[Proposition prop:basic-facts-homogeneity of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let gamble space $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ and variable $X:\Omega\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ be given.
  Then
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item $\overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}(cX) = c\, \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X$ for all $c\geq 0$ (1-homogeneity) when $\mathcal{Z}$ is arbitrage-free and scalable.
