[Theorem annLDPthm of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] Let $\tau$ be a resampling map, let $X = (X_n, n \in {\mathbb {N}})$ follow the law of the annealed RWCRE defined in (equation eq:annealed_rwcre of the paper), and let $\mu_n$ be the probability measure on ${\mathbb {R}}$ defined by $\mu_n(A): = {\mathbb {P}}(X_n/n \in A)$. 

If there is a function $\Lambda: {\mathbb {R}}\to {\mathbb {R}}$ that is strictly convex and such that
for all $\theta \in {\mathbb {R}}$,
\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        \lim_n \frac{1}{n} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta X_n}]&= \lim_n \sum_k \frac{T_{k,n}}{n} \frac{1}{T_{k,n}} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta Z_{T_{k,n}}}] = \Lambda(\theta).
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Then, $(\mu_n, n \in {\mathbb {N}})$ satisfies the large deviation principle in the sense of Definition III.6 of [dH00] with rate $n$ and function $I$ given by 
\begin{equation}
I(x) = \sup\{x \theta - \Lambda(\theta):   \theta \in {\mathbb {R}}\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

