	\end{equation}
	with the same uniformity and the same remainder estimate: for every $M$, truncating the
	exponent after $M$ terms leaves a relative error $O(N^{-M-1})$, uniformly on $K\times H$.  The
	coefficients $\widetilde A_k$ contain nothing but Bernoulli numbers and Bernoulli polynomials: no power
	of $t$ stands outside a $B_{k+1}(t)$.

