[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\ge 0}$ be a translation invariant, isotropic stochastic process on $\R^d$ satisfying Assumption~\ref{assump1}. Then for any nonnegative $f\in C^{1,\kappa}_c(\R^d)$,
		\begin{align*}
			\lim_{t\downarrow 0} \frac{\mathcal{R}^X_f(t)}{\mu(t)} = \int_{\R^d} |\nabla f(x)| dx,
		\end{align*}
		where $\mu(t)$ is defined in \eqref{eq:mu_sigma}. In particular, the above limit holds for all compactly supported smooth functions. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

