	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
 \alpha^*
    \]
    is a Quillen adjunction with homotopical right adjoint.
    \begin{proof}
        It is clear from the definitions that $\alpha^*$ preserves weak equivalences, while the construction as a transferred model structure in the proof of Theorem~(thm:G-gl-Sp-model-struct of the paper) makes it clear that $\alpha^*$ also preserves fibrations.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem wlln of arXiv:2604.12815, 'On ergodicity of the SAGA-LD algorithm\thanks{The author gratefully acknowledges the suppo'] Let $W_{n}$, $n\in\mathbb{N}$ be a real-valued process with $\alpha_{W}(n)\to 0$, 
$n\to\infty$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\lim_{V\to\infty}\sup_{n\geq 1}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}E[|W_{j}|1_{\{|W_{j}|\geq V\}}]\to 0,\ V\to\infty.	
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
E\left[\left|\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{n}[W_{j}-E[W_{j}]]}{n}\right|\right]\to 0,\ n\to\infty.	
\end{equation}
\hfill $\Box$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

