[Thm partialfilling of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\bm{t} \in \mathbb{Q}^{n-k}$. Let $\Phi\vert_{\bm{t}}$ be a blowdown of $\Phi$ along the multislope $\bm{t}$. If $\Phi\vert_{\bm{t}}$ is not an annulus, disk, or sphere suspension flow, then
    \begin{align} 
        Sl^\circ_{ \vert \bm{t}} \mathcal{Z}(\Phi) =  \mathcal{Z}(\Phi\vert_{\bm{t}}).
    \end{align}

