$(f\otimes f)^{\dagger}=f\otimes f$ for $f=f(X)$ self-adjoint. By (equation eq:itotable of the paper),
for adapted $a$,
\begin{equation}
  \big(f\,\mathrm{d} S\,f\big)\,a\,\big(f\,\mathrm{d} S\,f\big)
  =f\,\big[\mathrm{d} S\,(f a f)\,\mathrm{d} S\big]\,f=\tau\big(f a f\big)\,f^{2}\,\mathrm{d} t
  =\tau\big(af^{2}\big)f^{2}\,\mathrm{d} t,
\end{equation}
using traciality in the last step. Apply the free It\^o formula to $\varphi(X)=X^{n}$:
\[
  \mathrm{d} (X^{n})=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}X^{k}(\mathrm{d} X)X^{n-1-k}
