[Cor Theorem:SDEunderPh of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Under the same setting as in Theorem (GirsanovHTransform of the paper), $(\left\{ X_t \right\}_{[0,T]},\mathbf{P}^h)$ is a solution to the following SDE:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
   dX_t=b^h(t,X_t)dt&+\sigma(t,X_t)dB^h_t \\
   &+ \int_{|z|\leq 1}\gamma(t,X_{t-},z)\tilde{N}^h(dt,dz) 
   + \int_{|z|>1}\gamma(t,X_{t-},z)N(dt,dz),
   \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $b^h$ is as defined in (equation definition_b^h of the paper), $\left\{ B^h_t \right\}$ is a standard $\mathbf{P}^h$-Brownian motion in $\mathbb{R}^m$, and  $\tilde{N}^h(dt,dz)$ is the $\mathbf{P}^h$-compensated Poisson measure with intensity with $\nu^h$ as in (equation definition_nu^h of the paper).

