[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2609.04143, 'The Geometry of Real Anisotropic Bohnenblust--Hille Constants'] Let $m\ge2$, let $1\le i<j\le m$, and let $a,b\in[1,2]$. Assume
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1}a+\frac{1}b\le\frac{3}{2}.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 C_{\mathbf q_{i,j}^{(m)}(a,b)}^{(m)}
 =2^{\frac{1}a+\frac{1}b-1+(m-2)\left(\frac{1}{\min\{a,b\}}-\frac{1}{2}\right)}.
\end{equation}

[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] There is a lower semicontinuous inf-compact function
$\mathcal W:\mathsf X\to[1,\infty]$, and
constants $0<\rho<1$, $C<\infty$ such that
\begin{align}
 P_\tau\mathcal W&\le\rho\mathcal W+C,
 \\
 \mathbf{E}_z\left(L(z,Y)^p+\left|a_q(z, Y)\right|^p\right)&\le C\mathcal W(z)^{1/p},

\end{align}
where the constant $C$ in the second inequality may depend on $q$ through $a_q$. Moreover, 
\begin{align*}
      \sup _{\widehat{\mu} \in \mathfrak{I}} \int_{\mathsf X} \mathbf{E}_z\left[L(z, Y)^p+\left|a_q(z, Y)\right|^p\right] \widehat{\mu}(\dd z)<\infty.
\end{align*}

