[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2606.22044, 'Degenerate Stochastic Delay Modified Equation: Approximation of Stochastic Variance Reduce'] Define $ z _{k}^{y}$ as in (\ref{representation})  and let $\eta\in(0,1)$. Then, for any $0\leq k\leq m$, we have
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}| z _{k}^{y}|^{2}\leq C_{1}(1+|y|^{2}+\mathbb{E}|z_{0}|^{2})e^{C_{2}m\eta},
\end{align}
where $C_{1},C_{2}$ are certain positive constants that do not depend on $\eta$ or $m$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:bilinear of arXiv:2608.01253, 'The pseudo-quantum representation of \\finite reversible Markov chains'] The pseudo-wave and pseudo-density obey

\begin{equation}
\dot\Phi_z=K\Phi_z,\qquad \dot\rho_z=[K,\rho_z]=K\rho_z-\rho_zK.

\end{equation}

Moreover, for all $z$,

\begin{equation}
\rho_z^{T}=\rho_z,\qquad
\operatorname{Tr}\rho_z=\Phi_z^{T}\Phi_z=\Phi_0^{T}\Phi_0,
\qquad
\rho_z^{2}=(\operatorname{Tr}\rho_z)\,\rho_z.

\end{equation}

