[Proposition prop: total variation estimate explicit with epsilon of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $(k, \boldsymbol{\ell},\boldsymbol{\rho}) \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal P}} $. Recall that $F= 1-G$.  There exist $C_3 = C_3(k, \boldsymbol{\ell},\boldsymbol{\rho}) >0$ and $\varepsilon_3 = \varepsilon_3(k, \boldsymbol{\ell},\boldsymbol{\rho})>0$ such that the following holds. Let $\varepsilon\in (0,\varepsilon_3)$. Let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0} = (X_t^{(\varepsilon)})_{t\geq 0} $ be the FIT Markov chain with parameters $(k, \boldsymbol{\ell},\boldsymbol{\rho}, \varepsilon)$. Denote its stationary distribution by $\pi_\varepsilon$. For any $t\geq 0$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \left| \mathrm{d}^{(\varepsilon)}(t) - F(t)\right| \leq C_3\varepsilon.
    \end{equation}

