[Proposition prop:Xn_alpha of arXiv:2512.17736, 'Pathwise uniqueness by noise for singular stochastic PDEs'] Assume (A0 of the paper)--(A4 of the paper) hold  and let $x\in D({\mathcal A}^{-{\tilde \alpha}})$. Then, 
for every $T>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n \to \infty}\sup_{t\in (0,T]}t^{{\tilde \alpha}}\mathbb{E}
\|X_{n}(t)-X(t)\|_{\mathcal H}=0\,.
\end{equation}

