body:
[Lemma lem:radial-Bregman of arXiv:2608.30904, 'Entire monotone solutions of the anisotropic Allen--Cahn equation in dimension 5'] Let $F(n)=1$, $b=DF(n)$, and $\alpha\ge0$. For every
$\xi\in\mathbb R^4$,
\begin{equation}
B_H(\alpha n+\xi,\alpha n)
\ge \frac12(b\cdot\xi)^2.
\end{equation}
For every $\vartheta\in(0,1)$,
\begin{equation}
B_H(\alpha n+\xi,\alpha n)
\ge
\frac{1-\vartheta}{2}(b\cdot\xi)^2
+\frac{\vartheta\lambda}{2}|\xi|^2.
\end{equation}

[Lemma heat_kernel_from_Z_to_T of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] For any $x \in \mathbb{T}^d_L$, $n \in \mathbb N$, and $L \in \mathbb N^+$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        0 \le Q^n_L(o, x) - Q^n(o, \widecheck{x}) \le \frac{C \ n^{d + \alpha + 1}}{L^{d + \alpha}}
    \end{align*}
for some $C = C(\alpha, L)$.

