[Theorem th:covExpBound of arXiv:2412.04212, 'Rectangular Gilbert Tessellation'] Let $v,u\in \mathbb{R}^2$ be an arbitrary pair of points with  given arbitrary directions \mbox{$d_u, d_v$}. 
 There are positive constants $c$ and $\alpha$ such that for any $\lambda$
\begin{equation}
    \left|{\bf C}\left(A_{u,d_u}^{\pm}(t), A_{v,d_v}^{\pm}(t)\mid u,v  \in\mathcal{V} \right)\right|
\leq c e^{-{\alpha}{\sqrt{\lambda}}\|u-v\|_1}
    \end{equation}
    for all $t>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

