[Proposition goodrepeated of arXiv:2412.02087, 'The spectral distribution of random graphs with given degree sequences'] [Bounds on ``good" repeated edges] Suppose there are $r$ distinct ``good" repeated edges with multiplicities $\alpha_i\geq 2$. The following bound is achieved
    \begin{align*}
    \mathbb{E}\left[\left|H_1-\frac{1}{D-1}\right|^{\alpha_1}\left|H_2-\frac{1}{D-1}\right|^{\alpha_2}\cdots\left|H_r-\frac{1}{D-1}\right|^{\alpha_r}\right]\leq\frac{ (1+o(1))}{(D-1)^r}.
    \end{align*}

