[Definition def:Y of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Given a compact $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifold $(M,g)$, and any $I\subset (0,+\infty)$ bounded, we define the random variable $Y_M(I)$ and the constant $c_n$ as
    \begin{equation} 
Y_M(I):=\frac{1}{c_n\mathrm{Vol}^{n}(M)}\cdot \frac{\mathcal{L}_{\phi_{I}^M}(M)}{\lambda(\phi_I^M)}, \quad c_n:= \frac{s_{n-1}}{s_n\sqrt{n}}
    \end{equation}
where $\phi_I$ is defined as in (def:RRW of the paper) and $\lambda(\phi_I^M)$ is as in (eq:phiI of the paper).

