body:
[Theorem thm: heat_kernel_typical of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $d \ge 2$ and $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$ for some $\alpha > 0$.
    Then, there exists $C = C(Q) \in (0, \infty)$ and, for any $\kappa > 0$, there exists $c = c(\kappa, Q) > 0$ such that, for all $n \ge 1$ and $|x| \le \kappa r(n)$,
    \begin{align} 
        c \frac{1}{r(n)^d} \le Q^{n}(o, x) \le C \frac{1}{r(n)^d}.
    \end{align}
    where
    \begin{align} 
        r(n) := \begin{cases}
            \sqrt{n} &\text{ if } \alpha > 2, \\
            \sqrt{n \log n} &\text{ if } \alpha =2, \\
            n^{1/\alpha} &\text{ if } \alpha < 2.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align}
    Moreover, for every $\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $K$ such that
    \begin{align} 
        \sum_{m = 0}^n \sum_{\substack{y \in \mathbb Z^d \\ |y| > K r(n)}} Q^m(o, y) \le n \varepsilon.
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:equiv_discrete_path of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] For $C \in \mathcal{C}_{ar}^d$ the following two assertions are equivalent: 
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mu_C^{dis}(\mathbb{I}^d) > 0$, i.e., $C$ has non degenerated discrete component.
    \item $C\in \mathcal{C}_{ar,p}^d$.
    \end{enumerate}

[Lemma Lem: 1226 of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Given $X_1,X_2\in \mathcal{H}^d$ on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega,\mathcal{H},\hat{\mathbb{E}})$, let $\Gamma_i$ such that $X_i\sim \Gamma_i$, $i=1,2$. For any $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with Lipschitz constant $l_\phi$, define $v_i(t,x):=\sup_{y\in \Gamma_i}\phi(x+ty)$, $i=1,2$. Then for any $(t,x)\in \mathbb{R}_+\times \mathbb R^d$,
		\begin{equation*}
			|v_1(t,x)-v_2(t,x)|\leq tl_{\phi}\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_1-X_2|].
		\end{equation*}

