[Lemma l38 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] The sequence of measures ${\mathbb Q}^M_N = {\mathbb P}_{\nu^N} \circ (M^N)^{-1}$
on $D([0,T], {\mathscr D}'({\mathbb R} \times {\mathbb T}^{d-1}))$ converges, as
$N\to\infty$, to the centered Gaussian random field whose covariances
are given by
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
{\mathbb Q}^M \big[\, M_t(F) \, M_s(G)\,\big]\; & =\;
2\, (s\wedge t)\,  \int_{{\mathbb R}} d\vartheta \; 
\chi (\phi  (\vartheta)) \, \int_{{\mathbb T}^{d-1}} d\theta \;
(\partial_\vartheta F)(\vartheta, \theta)\,
(\partial_\vartheta G)(\vartheta, \theta)\,
\\
& +\; (s\wedge t)\, \int_{{\mathbb R}} d\vartheta \;
\widehat c_0(\phi  (\vartheta)) \,
\int_{{\mathbb T}^{d-1}} d\theta \; F(\vartheta, \theta)\,
G (\vartheta, \theta)\,   \;
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
for all $F$, $G$ in $C^\infty({\mathbb R} \times {\mathbb T}^{d-1})$ with compact
support. Here, ${\mathbb Q}^M$ stands also for the respective expectation.

