[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] For $x\in C$, $A\in\calX$ and $k\in\N^d$,

\begin{equation*}
\psi_k(x,A)=\psi^C_k(x,A\cap C)+\sum_{r\leqd k}\int_D g_D(r)(x,\dd y)\psi_{k-r}(y,A).
\end{equation*}

Consequently,

\begin{equation*}
\Psi_k(x,A)=\Psi^C_k(x,A\cap C)+\sum_{r\leqd k}\int_D g_D(r)(x,\dd y)\Psi_{k-r}(y,A),
\end{equation*}

where $\Psi^C=s_0*\psi^C$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

