[Defn 37 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] With notation as above, let $D$ be an $f$-big $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $X$.
We define the numerical vanishing order of $D$ along $v$ as
\begin{equation*}
v_{\num}(D/S)=
\inf_{S^0 \subset S} 
\inf \left\{ v(D') \middle|
\begin{gathered}
 \text{$D'$ is a $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $f^{-1}(S^0)$} \\
 \text{such that $D|_{f^{-1}(S^0)} \equiv_{S^0} D' \geq 0$}
\end{gathered} 
\right\}, 
\end{equation*}
where $S^0$ runs through all open neighborhoods of $c_{X}(v)$ in $S$.
By definition, $v_{\num}(D/S)$ only depends on the $f$-numerical equivalence class of $D$.

