[Lemma lem:Jordan2_lower_tail of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For the Jordan-$2$ ordering $\widehat{\sigma}_2$, there exists a positive constant $C$ such that for any $n\geq 1$, any vertex $v \in[n/4]$ and any $S\geq 1$, 

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}\Big(\widehat{\sigma}_2(v)\leq \frac{1}{S}v\Big) \leq  \frac{C}{S^2}.
    \end{equation}

[Corollary eq: spatialPA split up of arXiv:2411.02917, '\hspace*{2mm}\\[-16mm] Stein's Method for Spatial Random Graphs'] Let $(\Xi,\Sigma)$ be the graph constructed by the spatial preferential attachment model. 
Consider a function $h:\mathfrak{N}\times \mathcal{X}\times\mathfrak{N}_2\to\R_+$ that evaluates the edge structure of a (typical) vertex in the spatial preferential attachment model. Then  
\begin{align}
    \E\bigg[\int_{\mathcal{X}} h(\Xi-\delta_{(x,s)},(x,s),\Sigma\vert_{\langle \Xi-\delta_{(x,s)},(x,s)\rangle}) \, \Xi(\diff (x,s))\bigg] = \int_{\mathcal{X}} \E\bigl[h\big(\Xi,(x,s),(\Sigma_2^{<s},\Sigma_2^{>s})\big) \bigr] \, \alpha(\diff (x,s)),
\end{align}
where $\mathcal{L} \bigl( \Sigma_2^{<s},\Sigma_2^{>s} \bigm| \Xi, \Sigma \bigr) = \mathcal{L} \bigl( \Sigma_2^{<s} \bigm| \Xi_{s-}, \Sigma_{s-} \bigr) \otimes \mathcal{L} \bigl( \Sigma_2^{>s} \bigm| \Xi \bigr)$ is the product measure of outgoing and incoming edges for the additional vertex $(x,s)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:GeneralCheegerMixing of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] For all $\varepsilon > 0$ and $C > 0$, there exists a constant $\theta_0 > 0$ such that the mixing time of the modified chain satisfies
    \begin{equation*}
     \max_{\mathbf{x}\in \mathrm{Centre}(C)}t_{\textup{mix}}^{\textup{mod},\, \mathbf{x}}(\varepsilon) \leqslant \theta_0 \frac{n}{\Phi_{\ast}^{(n)}}
    \end{equation*}
    for all $n$ large enough.

