[Thm 10 of arXiv:2605.03528, '\bf Kolmogorov-Smirnov distance and discrepancies {\em versus} Wasserstein distances'] Let $q>p$ and $\mu$, $\nu$ two probability measures with finite $q$-moments. 
There exist real constants $\kappa_{p,q,d}>0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
{\cal W}_p^p (\mu,\nu)\le \kappa_{p,q,d}\big(M_{\frac{\mu+\nu}{2}}(q) \vee 1)\left\{\begin{array}{ll}

 D^\infty(\mu,\nu)^{\frac pd}  &\mbox{ if }p<\frac{dq}{q+d}\\
 D^\infty(\mu,\nu)^{1-\frac pq}  &\mbox{ if } \frac{dq}{q+d}<p \mbox{ and }p\neq d


 \end{array}
 \right.
\end{equation}
where $M_{\frac{\mu+\nu}{2}}(q)=\frac 12 \int_{\R^d} |\xi|^q (\mu+\nu)(d\xi)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

