[Lemma 67 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist positive constants $\mu_k,d_k,c_k>0$ such that for all $2\leq 2t<s$ and $\mathbf{a}$ additionally satisfying $[\mathbf{a}-s,\mathbf{a}+s]\subseteq [-n^{1/3}/4,n^{1/3}/4]$, and all $\varepsilon>0$ with $\alpha\coloneqq \log\varepsilon^{-1}$ satisfying
  \begin{equation}

    \mu_k\sqrt{\alpha(s/t)^{1/2}}\sqrt{s}<n^{2/3}/4,
  \end{equation}
  we have
  \begin{equation}

    \PP(\EE_{\cF_{[\mathbf{a}-s,\mathbf{a}+s]}}Z(\fB_{[\mathbf{a},\mathbf{a}+t],[\mathbf{a}-s,\mathbf{a}+s]},[\mathbf{a},\mathbf{a}+t])\leq \varepsilon)\leq e^{c_ks^3}e^{-d_k\alpha \sqrt{s/t}}.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor LDP_uniform_321 of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] For all $n \geq 1$, let $\sigma_n$ be a uniform random $321$-avoiding permutation of size $n$.
    Then, the permutons $\mu_{\sigma_n}^\diagup$ satisfy a large deviation principle at speed $n$ with rate function
    \[\overline{H}(\mu) := \left\{
    \begin{array}{ll}
      \inf_{0 \le \nu \le \mu_{\diagup}} H(\proj(\mu_{{\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=.4]
  \draw (0,0) -- (0.5,0) -- (0.5,0.5);
  \draw[thick,dotted] (0,0) -- (0.5,0.5);
\end{tikzpicture}}}+\nu)) & \textrm{if } \mu \in  \mathcal P_{\Av(321)},\\
      \infty & \textrm{otherwise.}
    \end{array}
\right.\]
The same LDP holds for the permutons $\mu_{\sigma_n}.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:physical-stability-comp of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Let $S\in L^\infty(\Omega\times\mathbb S^1)$ and $h\in L^\infty(\gamma_-)$ be real-valued, and let $f$ be the bounded mild solution of (equation eq:forced-physical-comp of the paper). Then
\begin{align}
 \nm f_\infty
 \le \abs h_{\infty,-}
 +C_\Omega\varepsilon^{-1}\nm S_\infty.

\end{align}
The constant depends only on $\Omega$, and not on $\varepsilon$, $S$, or $h$.

[Definition 89 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Let ${\bf L}^{\pm}$ denote the line parallel to the $y$-axis and with $x$-coordinate $x^\pm$, defined by
	\begin{flalign*}
		 x^-= \mathfrak{l}_{q'} (kN^{-1});\qquad     x^+= \bar{x} + N^{B\delta/9} \td_{\bar z}.  
	\end{flalign*}

