[Cor of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] Let $M$, $\zeta_t$, $\mu_t$ be as in Proposition (prop:long-term-est1 of the paper). Then, there exists a $\tau > 0$ such that 
    \begin{equation*} 
        \begin{split}
            \operatorname{var}_{\zeta_t} \biggl( \frac{\mu_t}{\zeta_t}\biggr) &\leq \operatorname{var}_{\zeta_0} \biggl( \frac{\mu_0}{\zeta_0}\biggr) e^{-\tfrac{\alpha_{\PI}}{2} t}, \qquad 
            \mathscr{H}_{\zeta_t} \biggl( \frac{\mu_t}{\zeta_t}\biggr) \leq \mathscr{H}_{\zeta_0} \biggl( \frac{\mu_0}{\zeta_0}\biggr) e^{-\tfrac{\alpha_{\LSI}}{2} t}
        \end{split}
    \end{equation*}
    for all $t \geq \tau$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 4 of arXiv:2609.00598, 'Supercritical mean--field limit for magnetized Hamiltonian dynamics'] Let $f_{\varepsilon}$ be a smooth solution to \eqref{magnetized vp with quasineutral scaling} with finite second velocity moment and sufficient decay in $\xi,$ and let $J_{\varepsilon}$ be given by \eqref{definition of current}. Then the pair $(\rho_{\varepsilon},J_{\varepsilon})$ satisfies the following equations{\rm:}
\begin{align}
&\partial_{t}\rho_{\varepsilon}+\mathrm{div}_{x}J_{\varepsilon}=0, 
