[Prop 9 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] Let $M>0$ and $(u,w)\in\mathcal{S}_{M,rad}$. Then $u\in\Sigma_a$ for $a:=M/|\mathbb{B}_R|$. In fact, with $v = \mathcal{K}[u-\langle u\rangle]$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
	u(x)\ge\min\left\{1,\exp\left(m^{-1}\big(\langle \phi'(u)\rangle-\|v\|_\infty\big)\right)\right\}>0\,,\quad x\in\bar{\mathbb{B}}_R\,.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $\phi'(u)=v+\langle \phi'(u)\rangle$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
	\|\nabla\phi'(u)\|_2^2=\int_\Omega \phi'(u)\left(u-a\right)\,\rd x\,.
\end{equation}

