\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 20 (Difference estimate) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Let two solutions remain in the bootstrap set and have the same composite
profile.  Put
\[
 \dot r=r^{(1)}-r^{(2)},\qquad
 \dot v=v^{(1)}-v^{(2)},\qquad
 \dot\psi=\psi^{(1)}-\psi^{(2)}
\]
and
\begin{equation*}
 B=e^{\phi^a}\int_0^1
 e^{\theta\psi^{(1)}+(1-\theta)\psi^{(2)}}\,\dd\theta.
\end{equation*}
Define
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
 \cE_{s-1,\eps}^{\rm diff}
 =\frac12\sum_{\abs\alpha\le s-1}\int_\Om
 \bigl(&n^{(1)}\abs{\pa^\alpha\dot v}^2
 +h_i'(n^{(1)})\abs{\pa^\alpha\dot r}^2\\
 &+B\abs{\pa^\alpha\dot\psi}^2
 +\eps^2\abs{\nabla\pa^\alpha\dot\psi}^2\bigr)\,\dd x.
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
Then
\begin{equation}
  \frac{\dd}{\dd t}\cE_{s-1,\eps}^{\rm diff}
  \le C\bigl(K_a+\mathfrak N_s^{(1)}+\mathfrak N_s^{(2)}\bigr)
  \cE_{s-1,\eps}^{\rm diff}. 
\end{equation}
The constant is independent of $\eps$.

