\[
  \Phi_s = Y(t,s)\,\mathcal{B}(s,X(s)).
\]
The bilinear map $(A,B) \mapsto AB^{*}$ sends $L_2(U,H) \times L_2(U,H)$ continuously into $L_1(H) \subset L_2(H,H)$, with $\norm{AB^{*}}_{L_2(H,H)} \leq \norm{AB^{*}}_{L_1(H)} \leq \lVert A \rVert_{L_2(U,H)}\allowbreak\lVert B \rVert_{L_2(U,H)}$; in particular $\gamma_t$ is trace class a.s. The Hilbert-valued Malliavin product rule therefore gives
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal{D}_r\gamma_t = \int_0^t \mathcal{D}_r(\Phi_s\,\Phi_s^*)\,\mathrm{d}s = \int_0^t \Bigl[(\mathcal{D}_r\Phi_s)\,\Phi_s^* + \Phi_s\,(\mathcal{D}_r\Phi_s)^*\Bigr]\,\mathrm{d}s,
\end{equation}
