body:
[Lem 50 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Consider all $\overline{N}\times K$ matrices with elements in $[k]_0$ such that: 
        \begin{enumerate}
            \item The first $m$ rows each start with $p$ and are larger than or equal to $s_i$ (in the lexicographical order);
            \item The number of $l$-digits in the first column of each of the last $N-n^{(1)}_p$ rows is $n_{ l}^{(1)}$ for all $l \in [k]_0 \backslash \{p\}$.
            \item There are at least $(y_{p,i}-y_1)$ rows equal to $s_i$;
            \item The number of $l$-digits in the $t$-th column is exactly $\overline{n}_{l}^{(t),m,\rem}$ for all $2 \leq t \leq K$ and $ l\in [k]_0$.
        \end{enumerate}
        Then for a uniformly random such matrix, the joint law of the first $m$ rows is that of $\widehat{\mathbf a}_i^{\rem,m}$ under $\mu_{\mathbf a_i} \lt( \cdot|\widehat{\mathbf{a}}_i\rt)$.

[Definition 37 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] We denote by $\Lip([0,T] \times W, \bar{W})$ the space of all continuous functions $f_0 : [0,T] \times W \to \bar{W}$ such that for some constant $L > 0$ we have
\begin{align*}
| f_0(t,y) - f_0(t,z) | \leq L |y-z| \quad \text{for all $t \in [0,T]$ and $y,z \in W$.}
\end{align*}

[Lemma lem:suff of arXiv:2412.03450, 'On intermediate levels of nested occupancy scheme in random environment generated by stick'] Assume that there exist constants $a_1, a_2>0$ and $r\in (\alpha, 1]$ such that, for all $v\in\mathbb{R}$ satisfying $|v|\leq a_1$,
\begin{equation}
|\mathbb{E} {\rm e}^{{\rm i}v\xi}-\Phi_\alpha(v)|\leq a_2 |v|^r.
\end{equation}
Then Assumption A holds with $\rho=0$ if $r>2\alpha$, $\rho=\delta$ for any $\delta>0$ if $r=2\alpha$ and $\rho=\lambda(2\alpha-r)$ for any $\lambda>1$ such that $\lambda (2\alpha-r)<\alpha$ if $r<2\alpha$.

