body:
[Corollary 20 of arXiv:2605.09706, 'A dyadic construction of a three-dimensional attractive point interaction Markov family'] Fix $L>0$. There exists a constant $C_L>0$ such that for all $T, \beta>0$ with $\beta\sqrt T\le L$, and all $x\in\R^3\setminus\{0\}$, the gradient of $Q_T^\beta(x)$ satisfies the following upper bound.
\begin{align} \nonumber
\big|\nabla Q_T^\beta(x)\big|
\,\le\,
C_L
\bigg[
\frac{1+\sqrt{T}}{|x|^2}\,\mathbf 1_{\{|x|\le \sqrt{T}\}}
\;+\;
\Big(\frac{1}{|x|}+\frac{1}{|x|\sqrt{T}}\Big)\,\mathbf 1_{\{|x|>\sqrt{T}\}}
\bigg]
\, e^{-4\pi\beta|x|}
\end{align}

