[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2603.28170, 'Stabilization time of finite configurations with a second class particle in discrete TASEP'] \begin{enumerate}
\item
For $p=1/2-\lambda/(2\sqrt n)$, there is a constant $c$ that depends only on $\lambda$ such that for all $n$ almost surely
\begin{equation}
\E\left(M-K\bigm|M\right)\le c\sqrt{n}.
