[Proposition prop:finite-dirichlet of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] Let $K$ be the transition kernel of the twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain on $[k]^n$. 
Let $S$ be a random row-stochastic $k\times k$ matrix with independent Dirichlet distributed rows, such that $S_{a,\bullet}\sim
 \mathrm{Dirichlet}\left(\frac\theta k,\ldots,\frac\theta k\right)$ for all $1 \leq a \leq k$. Let $S_1,S_2,\ldots$ be independent and identically distributed copies of $S$. Let
\[
 R_t:=S_1\cdots S_t \quad \text{and} 
 \quad R_0:=I_k.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
 K=\mathbb E[Q_S],
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 K^t=\mathbb E[Q_{R_t}]
 \qquad(t\ge0).
\end{equation}
Equivalently, if $(X_t)_{t\ge0}$ is the twisted Bose--Einstein chain, then the chain can be realized so that
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal L(X_t\mid S_1,\ldots,S_t,X_0=x)
 =
 \bigotimes_{r=1}^{n}(e_{x_r}R_t).
\end{equation}
Here $\mathcal L(X)$ denotes the law of a random variable $X$.

