[Lem 6 of arXiv:2607.24170, '\large\bf ON NON-MONOTONICITY OF LOGARITHMIC ENERGY\\ FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on $\C$ with $m_2(\mu)\leq C$.
If $\mathscr{D}_1,\ldots,\mathscr{D}_k$ are pairwise disjoint disks
of common radius
$r<1/2$, then
\begin{equation}
 \cE(\mu)\geq
 \left(\sum_{j=1}^k\mu(\mathscr{D}_j)^2\right)
 \log\frac1{2r}
 -\frac12\log2-C.
\end{equation}

