[Theorem thm:iterated_psi of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t \in [0, T]}$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued continuous semimartingale and let $\sigX[]$ denote its signature. Then,
    \begin{equation}
        \int_{0 \le s_1 \le \ldots \le s_n \le t} 
        \Big( \sigX[s_1] \otimes {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i_1}}} \otimes \sigX[s_1, s_2] \otimes \ldots \otimes {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i_n}}} \otimes \sigX[s_n, t] \Big) 
        \circ dX_{s_1}^{j_1} \ldots \circ dX_{s_n}^{j_n} 
        = {\bf\Psi}_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i_1}}}, \ldots, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i_n}}}}^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{j_1}}}, \ldots, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{j_n}}}} (\sigX[t]).
    \end{equation}

