[Lemma lemma_RN_time of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $t \in (0,\infty)$ and let $(\delta_m)_m$ be as Lemma (lemma_thinness_gamma_time of the paper). Then, almost surely, 
    \begin{equation} 
        \lim_{m \to \infty} \sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\frac{C_{\sigma}^{-k}h^k}{k!}\delta_m^{\frac{15k}{8}} \EEpmtime{m}{t} \big[\big( \sum_{x \in \Omega_{m,t}}\sigma_x\big)^k \big] = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} \frac{h^k}{k!}\int_{\Omega_t^k} f_t^{(\pm, k)}(x_1, \dots ,x_k) \prod_{j=1}^{k} dx_j < \infty
    \end{equation}
    where the functions $f_t^{(\pm, k)}:=f_{\Omega_t}^{(\pm,k)}$ are as in Theorem (theorem_spin_correlations of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm cont-XOR of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D\subset\mathbb C$ be a bounded, simply connected domain. Let $\tau$ be the continuum XOR-Ising model with free/free boundary conditions in $D$. Then, there exists a collection $(\mu_k)_{k=1}^\infty$  of measures supported on $(C_k)_{k=1}^\infty$ such that 
    \begin{align*}
        \tau = \lim_{N\to \infty}\ \sum_{k=1}^{N} \xi_{k} \mu_{k},
    \end{align*}
    where $(\xi_k)_{k=1}^\infty$ are i.i.d. symmetric signs. The sum converges almost surely in the Sobolev space $H^{s}(\mathbb C)$ for $s<-1$, under \emph{any ordering} that is independent of the collection of signs. Moreover, 
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item The excursions $C_k$ are connected and pairwise disjoint almost surely.
        \item Each measure $\mu_k$ is a deterministic function of the respective excursion $C_k$.
        \item The set of excursions $(C_k)_{k=1}^\infty$ is locally finite. That is, almost surely for any $\rho>0$ there are  finitely many $C_k$ with diameter greater than $\rho$. 
        \item For any continuous, bounded function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$, 
        \begin{align}
        \mathbb E\left[\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\mu_k,f)^2\right ]<\infty,
        \end{align} 
        and thus 
        \begin{equation}
           (\tau,f) = \lim_{N\to\infty} \sum_{k=1}^N \xi_k(\mu_k,f) \quad\text{in}\quad L^2(\mathbb P).
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}
    The same statement holds for\footnote{In this case, one needs to be careful to work in a domain $D$ whose boundary has small enough dimension (or, instead, restrict to the local Sobolev space $H^s_{loc}(D)$).} the XOR-Ising model with $+/+$ boundary conditions in $D$ by adding a symmetry-breaking (positive) measure $\mu_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:sec5-positive-radial-probes of arXiv:2607.18070, 'The Brownian loop-catcher'] Fix \(z\in\mathbb{D}\), \(\xi\in\partial\mathbb{D}\setminus\{-1,1\}\), and
\(\beta>\beta_*\).  There is a radial probe \(C_\beta\), a random radial
filling hull from \(\xi\) to \(z\), such that for every compact \(A\subset\ol\mathbb{D}\) with \(z,\xi\notin A\) and
\(\mathbb{D}\setminus A\) simply connected, we have
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb{E}\!\left[
 \mathbf 1_{\{C_\beta\cap A=\varnothing\}}
 e^{-\lambda m_\mathbb{D}(C_\beta,A)}\right]=|f_A'(\xi)|^\beta,
\end{equation}
where \(f_A:\mathbb{D}\setminus A\to\mathbb{D}\) fixes \(z,\xi\).

[Lem 18 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] There exists a universal constant $C_{d}$
depending only on the dimension, such that 
\begin{align*}
p_{\kappa}(s,\rho)\leqslant & C_{d}s^{-d/2}\exp\big(-\frac{(d-1)^{2}\kappa s}{4}-\frac{\rho^{2}}{4s}-\frac{(d-1)\sqrt{\kappa}\rho}{2}\big)\\
 & \ \ \ \times\big(1+\sqrt{\kappa}\rho+\kappa s\big)^{\frac{d-3}{2}}(1+\sqrt{\kappa}\rho)
\end{align*}
for all $s>0,\rho\geqslant0.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma operatorbound of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Given $B>0$, $\zeta\in\Gamma_B$ and $A_n\sim\operatorname{Sym}_n(\xi)$. 
Then for any $t>0$  we have
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left(\|A_n\|_{op}\geq (3+t)\sqrt{n}\right)\leq e^{-ct^{3/2}n}
\end{equation}
for some constant $c>0$ depending only on $B$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 8 (Sharpness of the cubic order) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] Fix \(0<a<b<\infty\) and \(R_0\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}\), and put
\(K_0=[a,b]\times\{0,\ldots,R_0\}\).  There are positive constants
\(A_-,A_+,B_-,B_+\), depending on \(K_0\) and \(\lambda\), such that
\begin{equation}
  A_-^q e^{-B_-q^3}
  \le \alpha_\lambda^{(q)}(K_0^q)
  \le A_+^q e^{-B_+q^3},
  \qquad q\ge1.
\end{equation}
Consequently, the power \(q^3\) in the uniform finite \(n\) estimate
\eqref{eq:main-uniform-bound} cannot be replaced by \(q^{3+\varepsilon}\),
for any \(\varepsilon>0\), while retaining a prefactor exponential in \(q\)
and constants independent of \(n,q\).

