[Theorem dimensional-criterion of arXiv:2412.08400, '\vspace{-1.0cm} Characterization of Exponential Families of \\ Lumpable Stochastic Matrice'] $\mathcal{W}_{\kappa}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})$ forms an e-family if and only if 
   \begin{equation*}
        \dim \left(\spann\left(\mathcal{G}_\kappa(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})\right) \oplus \mathcal{N}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}) \right)
        = \left| \mathcal{E} \right| + \left| \mathcal{Y} \right| + \left| \mathcal{D} \right| - \left| \mathcal{X} \right| - \sum_{(x,x') \in \mathcal{D}} \left| \mathcal{S}_x \right|.
   \end{equation*}

