[Lemma lem:TimeInMacro of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] For all $\delta > 0$, there exists a coupling $\mathbf{P}$ between $\mathbf{X}$ and $\mathbf{X}^{\textup{mod}}$ and a constant $c > 0$ such that for any $x \in {\mathrm{Macro}(\delta/(4d^2m^2))}$,
    \begin{equation*}
       \mathbf{P}(X_t = X^{\textup{mod}}_t \text{ for all } t \in [0,n^5] \, | \, X_0 = X^{\textup{mod}}_0 = x) \geqslant 1 - \exp\!\left(-c n\right)
    \end{equation*}
    for all $n$ large enough.

