body:
[Proposition 2 (Janssen test) of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] Let $g\in L^2(\mathbb R)$, $\|g\|_2=1,$ and let $\Lambda \subset \R^2$ be a lattice.
    The Gabor system $\G(g,\Lambda)$ is a frame for $L^2(\R)$ if
    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{\lambda^\circ \in \Lambda^\circ} |V_g g(\lambda^\circ)| < 2,
    \end{equation}
    where the notation $\Lambda^\circ$ stands for the adjoint lattice. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

