body:
[Lemma bound on alpha norm difference kernel ito mbm of arXiv:2604.27682, 'Multifractional Stable Motion with Random Hurst Exponent'] Fix $\alpha \in (0, 2)$, $0 < \underline{H} < \overline{H} < 1$ and a modulus of continuity $w : \mathbb{R}_{\geq0} \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$. There exists a constant $C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H})$ such that for all $\epsilon \in (0, 1)$, all functions $H:\mathbb{R} \to [\underline{H}, \overline{H}]$ admitting $w$ as a modulus of continuity and all $h \in (0, \frac12$),
\begin{align}
\int_{-\infty}^{t-\epsilon} \left|(t+h-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha} - (t-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha}\right|^\alpha \, dx &\leq C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H}) \, \epsilon^{\alpha(\underline{H}-1)} h^\alpha,  \\
\int_{t-\epsilon}^t \left|(t+h-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha} - (t-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha}\right|^\alpha \, dx &\leq C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H}) \, h^{\alpha(H(t)-w(\epsilon))},  \\
\int_t^{t+h} (t+h-x)^{\alpha H(x) - 1} \, dx &\leq C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H}) \, h^{\alpha(H(t)-w(h))} .
\end{align}

