body:
[Theorem thm:pythKL of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Assume that $\pi,G,P,M,\mathcal{X}$ satisfy the assumptions as stated in Theorem (thm:bisection of the paper), and $M \in \mathcal{D}(G,\nu)$. Assume that $P_{da}(G,\nu) \in \mathcal{D}(G,\nu)$. We have
	\begin{align*}
		D^\pi_{KL}(P \| M) &= D^\pi_{KL}(P \| P_{da}) + D^{\pi}_{KL}(P_{da} \| M).

	\end{align*}
	In particular, assuming $\pi$ is absolutely continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure so that we take $M = \Pi$, we see that
	\begin{align*}
		D^\pi_{KL}(P \| \Pi) \geq D^{\pi}_{KL}(P_{da} \| \Pi).
	\end{align*}

