body:
[Theorem THM713 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] Let $(\kappa, \theta)$ be a quasi-admissible pair. 
A quasi-regular and symmetric Dirichlet form $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ on $L^2(\overline{\Omega})$ is sandwiched between $(\mathbf{D},H^1_0(\Omega))$ and $({\mathscr E}^{\kappa,\theta},{\mathscr F}^{\kappa,\theta})$  if and only if there exists another quasi-admissible pair $(\kappa',\theta')$ with the properties
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
	&\Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'}\subset \Gamma_{\kappa,\theta},\quad \theta'\leq \theta|_{\Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'}\times \Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'}\setminus d},\\ &\kappa'\geq \kappa|_{\Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'}}+2(\theta-\theta')(dx,\Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'})|_{\Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'}}+2\theta(dx,\Gamma_{\kappa,\theta}\setminus \Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'})|_{\Gamma_{\kappa',\theta'}}
\end{aligned}\end{equation}
such that $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})=({\mathscr E}^{\kappa',\theta'},{\mathscr F}^{\kappa',\theta'})$.

