[Lemma lem:inverseforest of arXiv:2609.01672, '\textbf{All-Minors Matrix-Tree Theory for Superport Networks:\\ Completed Quotient-Inciden'] Let \(S,T\subseteq V\setminus\{g\}\) with \(|S|=|T|=r\). Then
\begin{align}
\det K^{-1}[S,T]
&=\frac{1}{\tau_c(G)}
  \sum_{F\in\mathcal{F}_{r+1}}
  \det Q_F[:,S]\notag\\
&\hspace{19mm}{}\times\det Q_F[:,T]w(F).

\end{align}
where \(\mathcal{F}_{r+1}\) denotes spanning forests with exactly \(r+1\) components.

