[Lemma lem:chim_diff of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d\ge 1$ and $m\ge 0$.
If $\chi ^{(m)} (p) < \infty$, then
\begin{align} 
\bigg ( \frac 1 { g_p ^2} - 3 \square_p ^{(m)} \bigg ) \chi ( \chi ^{(m)} )^2 - \chi ^{(m)}
\le  p\frac{\mathrm d  \chi ^{(m)} }{\mathrm d p}
\le \frac \Omega 2 \chi ( \chi ^{(m)} )^2 .
\end{align}

[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] Let $0\le p<(4a-1)/4a$. Then,
\begin{equation*}
\limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{S_n}{\sqrt{2n^{2a-1}\log\log n}}=\begin{cases}
	0\ \text{for}\ a>1,\ \text{a.s.},\\
	\frac{1}{\sqrt{3-4p}}\ \text{for}\ a=1,\ \text{a.s.}
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}

