[Prop 34 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] With the notations above,
for every $n\geq 1$ the following decomposition holds:
\begin{equation}

:\Phi^{n}: ~=~
\sum_{j=0}^{n} \dfrac{n!}{j! (n-j)!} Q_{n-j}(\ell_{a,b},V_{A_{a,b}})\,:\Phi_{D\setminus A_{a,b}}^{j} : \, ,
\end{equation}
where all the terms in the sum belong, as random variables,
to $L^{2}(d\PP,\sigma(\Phi),H^{-\eta}(\C))$
for every $\eta>0$.
In particular,
\begin{equation}

\E\big[ :\Phi^{n}: \big\vert A_{a,b}, \ell_{a,b}\big]
= Q_{n}(\ell_{a,b},V_{A_{a,b}}).
\end{equation}

