[Lemma lem:sandwich of arXiv:2601.10624, 'Source localisation in simple random walks'] Let $m \geqslant 8 /c(d)$. There are constants $k_0 = k_0(d) \in \mathbb{N}$ and $c_0 = c_0(d) > 0$ such that the following holds. Suppose that the event $\mathcal{A}_m$ occurs and $H$, $K$ are connected graphs such that
    \begin{equation*}
        G[0,b_k] \subseteq H \subseteq G[0,b_{k+2}]\quad \text{and} \quad G[0,b_l] \subseteq K \subseteq G[0,b_{l+2}]
    \end{equation*}
    for some $k,l \geqslant k_0$. Let $P \in \Diam(H)$. Then 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item one of the endpoints, $u$, of $P$ is contained in $G[0,b_0]$,
        \item the other endpoint of $P$ is contained in $G[b_{\lfloor kc_0 \rfloor},b_{k+2}]$, and
        \item there is $Q \in \Diam(K)$ which also has $u$ as one of its endpoints.
    \end{enumerate}

