body:
[Proposition prop:master-generating of arXiv:2609.02544, 'A finiteness theorem for geodesic Leech wheels'] A geodesic Leech labeling satisfies the following identity.
\begin{equation}
  \sum_{r=1}^{N}z^r
  =P_A(z)+P_B(z)+C_B(z)
  +\frac{P_A(z)^2-P_A(z^2)}2-C_A(z).
\end{equation}

[Prop vartheta = theta + epsilon of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] On the event $A_k$ defined in Lemma (Concentration for specific functionals of theta of the paper), for $n$ sufficiently large, we have,
\begin{equation}
        \vartheta_k(t) = (c_k(t)+\mu_k(t))\theta_k(t)+\epsilon_k(t),
    \end{equation}
    with $c_k(t):=\frac{1}{\|\theta_{k-1}(t)\|}$, $\epsilon_k(t) \in \Theta_{k-1}(t)+ \mathcal{E}_k(t)$, $\sup_{t \in [0,T]}\|\epsilon_k(t)\| \leq C_{k,T} \frac{\log(n)}{\sqrt{n}}$, and $\sup_{t \in [0,T]} |\mu_k(t)| \leq C_{k,T}\frac{\log(n)^{2(k-1)}}{n}$.

