[Lemma lem:lim_exist_1 of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] Let $\nu$ be any invariant measure for $\operatorname{GLPP}_c$. Then, if $f \sim \nu$, with probability one, one of the following holds.
    \begin{enumerate} [label=(\roman*), font=\normalfont]
        \item There exists $\theta > \frac{qr_c}{1-qr_c}$ such that 
        \begin{equation} 
        \lim_{k \to \infty} \frac{f(k)}{k} = \theta.
        \end{equation}
        \item Or, we have 
        \begin{equation} 
        \limsup_{k \to \infty} \frac{f(k)}{k} \le \frac{qr_c}{1-qr_c}.
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:x=v+eta(ej-ei) of arXiv:2606.10257, 'Downward conditional monotonicity gives survival and extinction for contact processes in r'] Let $x=v^*+\eta(e_j-e_i)$ for some fixed $\eta>0$ and fixed pair $i<j$. Assume that $T$ is strictly monotone, that $\alpha$ is increasing, and that, for every $\ell<i$,
