		Note that $n_{\alpha-r}-K\geq n_t+\ell tk\geq k$ by Lemma~\ref{lemma_bounds2}~(\ref{lemma_bounds2_nrnk}) and Lemma~\ref{lemma_nr}~(\ref{lemma_nr_sum}), so $K/(n_{\alpha-r}-K)=O(k)=O(M)$ by Lemma~\ref{lemma_bounds1}~(\ref{lemma_bounds1_v0}). We get $$\Delta_r^{(2)}+\Delta_r^{(1)}\geq(1-\delta-O(M^2/\alpha))(n_{\alpha-r}-K),$$ so the result ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:af7b757a8e13d13b653cdf03651fe63f4fdd7025da0f067ba4c700381ff70620","revision_digest":"sha256:5aff85fcb9e3c408c5eacfd1536d9de093eef4b6ed7f35de3fa22963cd4e228b","source_id":"arxiv:2608.07239","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

