[Theorem 2 (~\cite{Trip26Law}) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Let $n\geq 2, m\in \mathbb{N}$ and $p\in (0, 1)$. Then, for any $\pi\in S_n$, we have 
\begin{align*}
\nu_{n, m}^{(p)}(\pi)&= \frac{1}{m^n}[s^n](1+s)^{m}F_{\pi}(s)\;. 

\end{align*}
Here, and throughout this paper, we use $[u^n]P(u)$ to denote the coefficient of $u^n$ in the formal power series or polynomial $P$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

