body:
[Theorem lem:explicit-left-M of arXiv:2602.07920, 'On the position matrix of single-shelf shuffle and card guessing'] Let $n\ge 2$ and let $i\in \mathcal E_n$. For each
$1\le a\le n$, the $a$th coordinate of the left eigenvector
$\widetilde\zeta^{(i)}=(\widetilde{w}^{(i)})^\top B^{-1}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\widetilde\zeta^{(i)}(a)
= \frac{1}{i!(n-i)}\Bigl[
   (-1)^{\,i-a}\binom{i-1}{a-1}
 + (-1)^{\,n-1-a}\binom{i-1}{a-1-(n-i)}
 \Bigr],
\end{equation}
where, as usual, $\binom{m}{r}=0$ if $r<0$ or $r>m$.

