[Lemma lem:conditional-C0-strict of arXiv:2609.00556, 'Higgs--Demailly System and Positivity of Higgs Bundles'] Assume $f\geq-C_0$.  Then
\begin{equation}
 C^{-1}\operatorname{Id}_E\leq g\leq C\operatorname{Id}_E,
 \qquad c\operatorname{Id}_E\leq A_t\leq C\operatorname{Id}_E.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:AS of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d\ge1$.
Let $\Lambda \subset \mathbb Z^d$ be such that $0 \in \Lambda$ and $x \not \in \Lambda$. Then
\begin{align}

G_p(x) \le \sum_{\substack{y\in \Lambda \\ z \not \in \Lambda}} G_p(y) pD(z-y) G_p(x-z) .
\end{align}

[Proposition S62P of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] As $N \rightarrow \infty$, the sequence $\mathcal{L}^N$ converges weakly to some $\mathbb{N}$-indexed line ensemble $\mathcal{L}^{\infty}$ on $\mathbb{R}$, which satisfies the partial Brownian Gibbs property from [DM21]. Moreover, if $\mathcal{L}^{a,b,c}$ is as in [ED24a] for $\{a_i^+\}_{i \geq 1}, \{b_i^+\}_{i \geq 1}$ and $c^+$ as in the present statement, and $J_a^- = J_b^- = c^- = 0$, then
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}^{a,b,c} = \{f_q^{1/2} \cdot \mathcal{L}_i^{\infty}(f_q^{-1}t): i \in \mathbb{N}, t \in \mathbb{R}\},
\end{equation}
where the equality is in distribution as random elements in $C(\mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{R})$.

[Lemma avlemma1 of arXiv:2411.06089, '{\Large \bf Averaging principle for semilinear slow-fast rough partial differential equati'] Assume that the conditions in Theorem $(MainRes of the paper)$ hold.  Then for any $(x,y) \in \mathcal H \times \mathcal H$ and $\varepsilon >0$ small enough,
there exists a constant $C_T> 0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
     \mathbb{E}\big[\|X^{\varepsilon}\|_{\eta ,0}^4 \big] \leq  C_T (1+\|x\|_{\mathcal H}^4+\|y\|_{\mathcal H}^4),
     \end{equation}
and
   \begin{equation}
    \sup_{t\in[0,T]}\mathbb{E}\big[\|Y_{t}^{\varepsilon}\|_{\mathcal H}^4 \big]
    \leq  C_T(1+\|x\|_{\mathcal H}^4+\|y\|_{\mathcal H}^4).
	\end{equation}

