[Lemma unregu of arXiv:2411.15881, 'Stable Approximation for Call Function Via Stein's method'] For any $g\in{\rm Lip}(1)$ and let $f_{g}$ be the solution to equation (equation stablestein of the paper), then for any $y\in(-\infty,\infty)$, we have
\begin{align}
\|f'_{g}\|_{\infty}\leq\alpha, \qquad \|f''_{g}\|_{\infty}\leq4\eta_{2,\alpha,\delta},
\end{align}
where $\|f\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}}|f(x)|$ for any function $f:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$.

