[Definition def:u_pm of arXiv:2512.17808, 'Zeros of polynomial powers under the heat flow'] We define the two solutions to $\frac u {\sqrt t} +\frac{\sqrt t} u =\frac z{\sqrt t}$ by
	\begin{align}

		u_{t}^{\pm}(z):=\frac{1}2(z\pm\sqrt{z^2-4t}), \quad z\in\mathbb{C}\setminus \big( (-\infty,-2\sqrt t]\cup [2\sqrt t,\infty) \big),
	\end{align}
	where we choose the branch of the root such that $u_t^+(z)\sim z$ as $|z|\to\infty$ with $z\in \mathbb{C}_+$, and $u_t^-(z)\sim z$ as $|z|\to\infty$ with $z\in \mathbb{C}_-$, respectively.
	If $t=1$ we will denote the solutions by $u^{\pm}(z):=u_1^\pm(z)$.

[Lem eq:diffHa of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] Let $\rho: {\mathbb R}^{d_2} \mapsto {\mathbb R}$ and $h: {\mathbb R}^{d_1} \mapsto {\mathbb R}$ be differentiable. Then the function
$$
   H({\bm x}, {\bm y}) := [\rho({\bm y})]^m h\left(\frac{{\bm x}}{\rho({\bm y})} \right)
$$
satisfies the following relations
\begin{equation} 
  \rho({\bm y})  \partial_{y_i} H = \partial_{y_i} \rho({\bm y}) \left( m  - {\langle} {\bm x},\nabla_{\bm x}{\rangle} \right) H, \quad 1 \le i\le d_2,
\end{equation}
and, in particular, 
 \begin{equation} 
  \rho({\bm y})  {\langle} {\bm y}, \nabla_{{\bm y}}{\rangle}  H = {\langle} {\bm y}, \nabla_{{\bm y}}{\rangle} \rho ({\bm y}) \big( m  - {\langle} {\bm x},\nabla_{\bm x}{\rangle} H \big). 
\end{equation}

