    Applying (equation eq:GoodOtter of the paper) with $\bU = [\bM_{p,\beta}, \zeta_{p,\beta}] \bmod p,\beta$ by taking $m=1$ and $k=0$ yields (equation eq:TediousPop2 of the","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:edc6f0cb49bad68389b6bafd629347af52f283ef38e7eaea2f31cd1fca80058a","revision_digest":"sha256:5e114cc365739d0cd0f51a6ff8cf8c66d1ee305751fcc4e8653695818db3d032","source_id":"arxiv:2603.26932","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

