[Lemma lem_animal of arXiv:2608.08532, 'Constrained Maximum Weight Paths in Random Geometric Graphs'] Suppose the conditions in Theorem~(thm_path of the paper) hold and  let~\(F_c(.)\) be the edge weight ccdf. There are constants~\(\delta_1,\delta_2 > 0\) such that for any~\(x,y > 0\) and~\(Q \geq 1,\)
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left(\max_{\cal P} N_{edge}\left(x,{\cal P}\right) \geq y\right) \leq e^{\delta_1Q \Lambda} \cdot e^{-y} + e^{-\delta_2 N}, 
\end{equation}
where~\(\Lambda := \max(1,t^2N^2F_c(x))\) and the maximum is over all~\(t-\)animals of size~\(Q\) containing the origin. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition Intersection patterns/shapes of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Given two shapes $\tau_1$ and $\tau_2$ that are composable, we define an intersection pattern for $\tau_1$ and $\tau_2$ to be a non-empty set $I \subseteq \left(V(\tau_1) \setminus V_{\tau_1}\right) \times \left(V(\tau_2) \setminus U_{\tau_2}\right)$ of intersection edges where each vertex is incident to at most one edge. Whenever we have an intersection edge $e = \{a,b\}$ (between vertices of the same type), this means that when we consider maps $\sigma: V(\tau_1) \cup V(\tau_2) \to [n]\cup [d] $, we have the restriction that $\sigma(a) = \sigma(b)$.

We define $\tau_{I} = \tau_{I}(\tau_1\cdot \tau_2)$ to be the shape obtained from $\tau_1$ and $\tau_2$ as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Start with the properly concatenated shape $\tau_1\circ \tau_2$;
\item For each intersection edge $e = \{a,b\}$, merge $a$ and $b$ together into one vertex.
\end{enumerate}

[Definition eq:defannealedgaussian of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] A potential $V : \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}} \to \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ is said to be an annealed Gaussian potential if the map $k \mapsto k^2 e^{-V(k)}$ is summable over $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ and if there exists a Borel probability measure $\mu_V$ on $(0,\infty)$ such that, for any $x \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$,

\begin{equation} 
    e^{-V(x)} = \int_0^\infty e^{- \frac{x^2}{2J}} \mu_V(d J).
\end{equation}

[Lemma le:scalinv of arXiv:2411.09058, 'Time-dependent averages of a critical long-range stochastic heat equation'] For any radius $R>0$,
    any time $t\geq 0$, and any $\varepsilon >0$, we have
\begin{equation}
            u_{t}(B_R)=\varepsilon^{-d/2} u_{\varepsilon t}(B_{\sqrt{\varepsilon}R}) \quad \text{in law}.
    \end{equation}

[Definition banachmazur of arXiv:2411.14177, '\textbf{Invariant Sublinear Expectations}'] Let $\ell_{\infty}$ be the space of all bounded sequences. A positive linear functional $\Lambda: \ell_{\infty} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is a Banach-Mazur limit if
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\quad \Lambda(\boldsymbol{e})=1$, where $\boldsymbol{e}=(1,1,1, \ldots)$,
        \item $\quad \Lambda\left(x_1, x_2, \ldots\right)=\Lambda\left(x_2, x_3, \ldots\right)$ for each $\left(x_1, x_2, \ldots\right) \in \ell_{\infty}$.
    \end{enumerate}

[Theorem 4 (Exact CNN representation of the slope change classifier) of arXiv:2609.00402, '2609.00402'] Let \(T\geq5\), \(\mathcal I=\{3,\ldots,T-2\}\), and \(B=2(T-4)\). Let $\bm L=(1,\ldots,1)$, $\bm k=\{k_{b,1}=T:b=1,\ldots,B\}$, $\bm{\mathcal P}=
\{(\operatorname{Pool}_{b,1},w_{b,1},s_{b,1})
=(\operatorname{Id},1,1):b=1,\ldots,B\}$, $\bm C=\{C_{b,0}=1,C_{b,1}=1:b=1,\ldots,B\}$, $\bm m=(1,\ldots,1)$. For every \(\lambda>0\), there exists $f_{S,\lambda}\in
\mathcal F_{\mathrm{CNN}}
(T,B,\bm L,\bm k,\bm{\mathcal P},\bm C,\bm m)$ such that $\mathbb I\{f_{S,\lambda}(\bm X)>0\}
=\mathbb I\{S(\bm X)>\lambda\}$ for every $\bm X\in\mathbb R^T$. Consequently, $h_{S,\lambda}\in \mathcal H_{\mathrm{CNN}} (T,B,\bm L,\bm k,\bm{\mathcal P},\bm C,\bm m)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 90 (Uniqueness on successive time intervals) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $\Xi$ satisfy Definition~\ref{def:Xi-assumptions}, and let $Z,\widetilde Z\in\mathcal Z_T$ be two
fixed points with the same Cauchy data.  Then $Z=\widetilde Z$ on $[0,T]$.
Let $I=[t_0,t_1]\subset[0,T]$ and suppose the two solutions agree
on $[0,t_0]$.  With $R$ larger than their two $\mathcal Z_T$ norms, the
translated difference satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \|Z-\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_I}
 \le \varpi_{\Xi,R}(|I|)
 \|Z-\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_I},
\end{equation}
where, with $\delta_{\mathrm{loc}}:=\min\{\delta,1/4\}>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \varpi_{\Xi,R}(h)
 \le C_{\Xi,R}h^{\delta_{\mathrm{loc}}}
 +C_R\omega_{\mathrm{cen},\Xi}(h)
 \longrightarrow0
 \qquad(h\downarrow0).
\end{equation}
Here $\mathcal Z_I$ denotes the translated solution norm on
$I$, with zero Cauchy data at the left endpoint for the difference.

[Satz thm:powers-bernoulli of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d,k\in\mathds{N}$, $s,\alpha,\beta,\gamma\in\mathds{R}$, $p,q\in (0,\infty]$, $r\in (0,\infty)$, and $\mu,\nu \in (-\infty,0]$.
Assume that $a$ follows a Besov--Bernoulli{} prior and $f$ follows a Besov--Bernoulli{} prior, both with parameters $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\mu,\nu,k)$ and template random variable $X$, satisfying
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases} \:\exists\: \eps>0:\,\mathds{E}\bigl[\left\lvertX\right\rvert^{(1+\eps)\max\left\{r,p\right\}}\bigr]< \infty&\text{if }p\in (0,\infty),\\
\:\exists\:  R>0:\, \left\lvertX\right\rvert\stackrel{a.s.}{\leq}R&\text{if }p=\infty.\end{cases}
\end{equation}
If Property A'' is satisfied, then $\mathds{E}[\left\lVerta\right\rVert_{b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)}^r]<\infty$.
If Properties A'' and B are satisfied, then $\mathds{E}[\left\lVertf\right\rVert_{B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)}^r]<\infty$.
In particular, $f$ belongs to $B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)$ almost surely.

