[Theorem thm.speis of arXiv:2504.19553, 'Extremal Ising Gibbs States on Lobachevsky lattices'] Let ${\rm IC}_G$ be the isoperimetric constant of the {connected, transitive and locally finite graph $G$}. If the following sparsity condition holds
\begin{equation}
\delta_{\rm max} < \frac{1}{2}\; {\rm IC}_G
\end{equation}
then, at sufficiently low temperature, for any $\omega \in \Omega_{\rm GS}(\delta_{\rm max})$, the Gibbs measure $\mu^{\omega}$ of the Ising model on $G$, obtained as weak limit with boundary condition $\omega$, is {well-defined} and {extremal}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:y(t)-properties-ER of arXiv:2411.12076, 'Explicit solutions of the SI and Bass models on sparse Erd\H{o}s-R\'enyi and regular netwo'] Let~$y_{\rm Bass}(t)$ be the solution of~(equation eq:y-ER-Bass of the paper). Then 
		\begin{equation}


			\frac{dy_{\rm Bass}}{dt}<0, \quad t>0   \qquad \text{and} \qquad \lim_{t \to \infty} y_{\rm Bass} = 0.
		\end{equation}
		In particular, $0<y_{\rm Bass}(t)<1$ for $t>0$.

