[Proposition pr:second-moment of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $\lambda =7/8$, and recall from (equation eq:beta-lambda-N of the paper) that $\beta_{\lambda,N}\sim N^{-1/8}$. Then, for every $t\ge 0$ and sequence $\mathbf x^N\in \mathbb{Z}^2$ such that $N^{-1/2}\mathbf x^N\to \mathbf z\in \mathbb{R}^2$, 
   \begin{equation}\mathbb{E}\bigg[ \prod_{j=1,2}\mathfrak H_{\beta_{\lambda,N},N}(t,x_j^N,1)\bigg] \xrightarrow[N\to \infty]{} \mathbf E_{(z_1,z_2)}^{{\rm BM    }^{\otimes 2}}\bigg[ \exp\set{{\frac12}  L_t^{W^1-W^2} } \bigg]\; \text{,}\;\; 
   \end{equation}
   where $1\in \ensuremath{\mathcal C}_b(\mathbb{R})$ in $\mathfrak H_{\beta_{\lambda,N},N}(t,x_j^N,1)$ indicates the constant function equal to one.

