[Proposition 50 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Denote by $\ma{M}_n^{(T)}\equiv \ma{M}_n^{G,(T)} $ the upper-left $n_0\times n_0$ corner of $\ma{M}_n$. Set
    \begin{align*}
    \mathsf{K}_n^{(T)}(x,y)\equiv\mathsf{K}_n^{G,(T)}(x,y) = \sigma_n^{-1}m_n\Big[\big(\ma{M}_n^{(T)}\big)^{-1}\Big]_{\lceil x m_n\rceil, \lceil y m_n\rceil} \ind(0<x, y\le T),
\end{align*}
    then for any fixed $T>0$, there exists a coupling so that $\|\mathsf{K}_n^{(T)}-\mathsf{K}_{\Ai}^{(T)}\|_{2} \to 0$ a.s.~as $n\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:SRWoptimal of arXiv:2601.10624, 'Source localisation in simple random walks'] We have
    \begin{equation*}
        \liminf_{n\to\infty} \inf_{v \in \mathbb{Z}^d} \mathbb{P}_v\big(\Psi\big(G_n^{\mathbb{Z}^d}\big) = v\big) = 1/2 - O(1/d) \ \text{ as } \ d \to \infty.
    \end{equation*}
    Moreover, for every estimator $\Phi$, we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \limsup_{n\to\infty} \inf_{v \in \mathbb{Z}^d} \mathbb{P}_v(\Phi(G_n^{\mathbb{Z}^d}) = v) = 1/2 - \Omega(1/d) \ \text{ as } \ d \to \infty.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

