body:
[Lemma 48 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] Fix $\delta>0$. The following holds almost surely. For all $t\in \RR$ and $\theta\in [0,\infty]$ admitting a $\theta$-directed semi-infinite geodesic $\Gamma^{t}$, and for all $m$ large enough, we have 
  \begin{equation}

    \Gamma^t\cap \{m\}_{\RR}\subseteq [\theta m-m^{2/3+\delta}, \theta m+m^{2/3+\delta}].
  \end{equation}

