[Lemma l2-02 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a cylinder function $f$. Then, there exists a finite constant
$C_1 = C_1(f)$ such that
\begin{align*}
& {\mathbb E}_{\nu^N} \Big[\,
\int_0^t \,\Big|\, \sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} J_x \,
[\, f(\tau_x \eta^N(s)) - R_f(x) \,]  \,\Big| \,  \, ds \, \Big] \\
&\qquad \le\;
\frac{1}{\lambda} \, \int_0^t  \big\{\, H_N(f^N_s)
\,+\, \log 2 \, \big\} \, ds
\;+\; 
C_1 \, \lambda\, e^{C_1 \, \lambda\,  \Vert  J \Vert_\infty}
\, \sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} J_x^2 \; t
\end{align*}
for every function $J:{\mathbb T}^d_N \to {\mathbb R}$, $t>0$, $N\ge 1$,
$\lambda>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem recur:upperBoundThreeSeq of arXiv:2607.09841, 'Mixing and cutoff for the systematic scan dynamics of the mean-field ferromagnetic Potts m'] Let $\{x_t\}_{t \geq 0}$ be a sequence of positive real numbers, 
such that $x_t \leq n$ for $t < n$, and for $t \geq n$
\begin{align*}
    x_t &= \frac{\beta}{nq}\sum_{i = t-n}^{t-1} x_i + C \sum_{i = t-n}^{t-1} \gamma_n^{2i} + C.
\end{align*}
where $C > 0$ is a constant. Then, there exists a constant $\hat C > 0$ such that for all $t \geq 0$
\begin{align*}
     x_t  \leq \hat C n \gamma_n^t + \hat C.
\end{align*}

