[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2606.08115, '2606.08115'] Let condition (C) be valid for a two-dimensional random walk $\left\{ \ov{S}_n\right\}$. Let $D \subset K$ be a measurable bounded set such that $\delta := \mathrm{dist}\left(D, \partial K\right) > 0$. Then for any $s \in (0, 1/2)$ and $\ov{x} \in \mathcal{X}_V$ 
$$\lim_{T \to \infty}\pr_{\bfx}^{+}\left( \ov{S}_T + \ov{x} \in \sqrt{T}D, \exists j > T: \ov{S}_j + \ov{x} \notin U_{T, s}\right) = 0,$$
 where
\begin{equation}

U_{T, s} = \left\{ \ov{x} \in K : \mathrm{dist}\left(\ov{x}, \partial K\right) > T^{1/2 - s}\right\}.
\end{equation}

