body:
[Lem Lyap1 of arXiv:2412.03560, 'Non-asymptotic entropic bounds for non-linear kinetic Langevin sampler with second-order s'] Under Assumption~(assu:LyapunovRd of the paper), assuming furthermore that $3\lambda < r$, there exists a constant $C\in\mathcal C(\mathfrak{p})$  such that, for any $N\in\mathbb N$, $\mathbf{z}\in\mathbb R^{2dN}$ and $i\in\llbracket 1,N\rrbracket$,
\begin{multline*}
\varphi(\bar{z}_i)   \leqslant  \varphi(z_i) + \rouge{h \left( -  \frac{r\alpha }4   |x_i|^2 + \left( \frac{5}{4}\alpha+ \frac{\lambda}2\right) |v_i|^2\right)} + \magenta{\frac{h \lambda}2(1+\alpha)m^2(\mathbf{x})} \\
+ \bleu{ hd \left( \alpha K + \frac{\alpha M^2}{r} + \frac{M^2}{\alpha}\right)  + C h^2 \left( |z_i|^2 + m^2(\mathbf{z})+d\right)  }\,.
\end{multline*}

