[Proposition of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Consider the sequence of FIT Markov chains $((W^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0})_{n\geq 8}$ defined above. For every $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and every $c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $, as $n\to \infty$ we have 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{d}^{(n)}(\left\lfloor n + c n^{\alpha} \right\rfloor) \to \begin{cases}
            1 & \text{ if } c\leq 0 \\
            1-\alpha & \text{ if } c>0. 
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation}

[Theorem thm:thm1 of arXiv:2607.26551, 'An RDT based confirmation of Lehner's formula for Kronecker-Gaussian matrices'] For large $n\in{\mathbb N}$ and fixed $k,l\in{\mathbb N}$, let $G_{i}\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times n}$ and $G_{i}^{(1)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k\times n},i=1,\dots,l$ be independent  standard normal matrices. For deterministic $A_i\in{\mathbb R}^{k\times k}$ such that $A_i=A_i^T\succeq 0,i=1,\dots,l$ and fixed $R$ such that $\mbox{Tr}(R^TR)=1$, let $F_i$ be as in 
((eq:inteq1ab0b0 of the paper)). Set
\begin{eqnarray}

 L & = &  
 \max_{X\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times k},X^TX=I} \sum_{i=1}^{l}  \sqrt{2}\mbox{Tr}(G_i^{(1)} X F_i)   .
\end{eqnarray}
Let $\xi$ be as in ((eq:kronrep6 of the paper)) and ((eq:inteq1ab0 of the paper)).  One then has  
\begin{eqnarray}

\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi   \leq  \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} {\mathbb E} L,
\end{eqnarray}
with the righthand side being the so-called random dual.

