\[
D_1 D_2\cdots D_m-J_n = (D_1- J_n)(D_2- J_n)\cdots (D_m- J_n)
\]
is proved by induction. By the submultiplicative property of the spectral norm $\|\cdot\|_2$, we have
\begin{equation}
\|D_1 \cdots D_m-J_n\|_{2} \leq \|D_1- J_n\|_{2}\cdots \|D_m-J_n\|_{2}.  
\end{equation}
Moreover, Birkhoff's theorem and the permutation invariance of both $J$ and the spectral norm ensures that 
\begin{align}
\|D-J_n\|_{2} &=  \bigg\| \sum_{i} \alpha_i (P_i -J_n) \bigg\|_2 \notag\\
&\leq \sum_{i} \alpha_i \|P_i-J_n\|_2 \\
&= \sum_{i} \alpha_i \|I_n-J_n\|_2 = 1, \notag
\end{align}
for all $D\in\ds$. Here, we used the easily verified identity $\|I_n-J_n\|_2=1$. 

