[Theorem thm:main-upper-bound of arXiv:2510.11015, 'An interpretable universal bound for multiserver queues via a leave-one-out technique'] Consider the $GI/GI/n$\xspace queue with homogeneous servers under the FCFS policy, whose service-time and interarrival-time distributions satisfy Assumptions~(assump:bdd-exp-remain of the paper), (assump:non-lattice of the paper) and (assump:modified-ggn-stable of the paper). When the load $\rho < 1$, let $\pi$ be the unique stationary distribution of the system. Then the steady-state mean queue length, $\Ep{\pi}{Q}$, is bounded as
    \begin{equation}

        \begin{aligned}
            \Ep{\pi}{Q} &\leq \frac{\rho\textnormal{Var}\left[\Lambda A\right] + \textnormal{Var}\left[\mu S\right] + 1-\rho}{2(1-\rho)} + \min\Big(n, \frac{1}{1-\rho}\Big) \Big(R_{s}^{\max} - \frac{1}{2} \mathbb{E}\left[(\mu S)^2\right]\Big) \\
            &\mspace{23mu} + \Big(\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[(\Lambda A)^2\right] - R_{a}^{\min}\Big).
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem non-expl of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Assume that Items~(item:mutual-independence of the paper) and~(item:finiteness of the paper) of Assumption~(ass:gen-ass of the paper) are satisfied, and for $\alpha > 0$, we have 
\begin{equation} 
\sum_{j=1}^{\infty} \E{e^{-\alpha \sum_{i=1}^{j} X_{i}}} < 1.
\end{equation} 
Then, for any $t >0$, $|\mathscr{T}_{t}| < \infty$.

