body:
[Prop Prop_UniversalBundleOfZ2ZSpinors of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] The \defined{universal bundle of $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$ spinors}
  \begin{equation*}
    {\mathbf{E}}_{0} \coloneq \ker \mathbf{res} \subseteq \mathbf{E}
  \end{equation*}
  is a tame Fréchet space subbundle.
  Moreover,
  the exact sequence
  \begin{equation*}
    {\mathbf{E}}_{0} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{E} \stackrel{\mathbf{res}}{\twoheadrightarrow} \mathbf{G}
  \end{equation*}
  of tame Fréchet space bundles locally splits;
  that is:
  for every $({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}]) \in \mathbf{Dir} \times \mathbf{Ram}$
  there are an open neighbourhood $({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}]) \in \mathscr{U} \subseteq \mathbf{Dir} \times \mathbf{Ram}$ and
  a map of tame Fréchet space bundles $\mathbf{ext} \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace \mathbf{G}|_\mathscr{U} \to \mathbf{E}|_\mathscr{U}$ satisfying $\mathbf{res} \circ \mathbf{ext} = \mathbf{1}$.

[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2609.00285, 'Multicrossing complex of knot and secant classes'] Let links $L=K_1\cup\cdots\cup K_m$ and $L'$ obtained from $L$ by switching a crossing on components $K_p$ and $K_q$, $1\le p,q\le m$. Then for any $i\ne j\ne k\ne i$
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $I^-_{ijk}(L)=I^-_{ijk}(L')$;
    \item $I^-_{iji}(L)-I^-_{iji}(L')=\left\{\begin{array}{cl}
        1, & \{i,j\}=\{p,q\}, \\
        0, &  \mbox{otherwise}
    \end{array}\right.\pmod 2$.
\end{enumerate}

