[Prop positiveSignFeatureLaplace of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Fix $\beta>0$ and assume that
\begin{align}
2\beta\|T_q\|_{\mathrm{op}}<1,
\qquad
\sup_{M\ge1}{\mathbb{E}}\brak*{e^{\beta\mathsf W_M(q)}}<\infty,
\qquad
\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d}} e^{aD(x)}\,\mathop{}\!\mathrm d\mu(x)<\infty
\end{align}
for some $a>0$.  Then there is a finite constant $C$ such that, for every $N\ge1$,
\begin{align}
\left|
{\mathbb{E}}\brak*{e^{\frac\beta2\mathsf W_N(q)}}
-\mathrm{det}_2\pa*{\mathrm{Id}-\beta T_q}^{-1/2}
\right|
\le C N^{-1/2}.
\end{align}
For fixed $\beta$ and $a$, the constant may be chosen to depend polynomially on $1+\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d}} e^{aD(x)}\,\mathop{}\!\mathrm d\mu(x)$, with coefficients depending only on the subcritical margin $1-2\beta\|T_q\|_{\mathrm{op}}$, $\|T_q\|_{\mathrm{HS}}$, and the uniform exponential moment in (equation eq:positiveSignFeatureAssumptions of the paper).

