[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2606.24485, 'On the convex hull of a planar Brownian bridge with a random Gaussian endpoint'] For every $\sigma \in [0,1]$, one has
	\begin{equation}
		\int_0^1 t(1-t)\arctan\ob{\sigma\sqrt{\frac{1-t}{t}}}\D t
		=
		\frac{\pi\sigma(4\sigma^2+9\sigma+3)}{48(1+\sigma)^3}.
	\end{equation}

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:3ef1ab6749768898c8b316f8d22337cfd9acbfc3bbeed01e4a9abf940fc7e9bf","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/3e/3ef1ab6749768898c8b316f8d22337cfd9acbfc3bbeed01e4a9abf940fc7e9bf.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:22cceca33fefa50d8ddca72597f2f865b0256db5e68b3f00d1ce609b3b353f3d","bundle_entry_key":"2606-24485-lemma-11-a2","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_057","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_057.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-24485-lemma-11-a2","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Denote the integral in the statement of the lemma by $I(\sigma)$. Using the substitution \( x = \sqrt{(1-t)/t} \) we conclude that
	\begin{align}
		I(\sigma) & =
		\int_0^1 t(1-t)\arctan\ob{\sigma\sqrt{\frac{1-t}{t}}}\D t \\
		          & = 2\int_0^\infty
		\frac{x^3}{(1+x^2)^4}\arctan(\sigma x)\D x.
	\end{align}
	Differentiating with respect to $\sigma$ gives
	\begin{equation}
		I'(\sigma)=
		2\int_0^\infty
		\frac{x^4}{(1+x^2)^4(1+\sigma^2x^2)}\D x.
	\end{equation}
	To continue, rewrite the numerator as
	\begin{equation}
		x^4 = \ob{(1+x^2) - 1}^2 = (1+x^2)^2 - 2(1+x^2) + 1,
	\end{equation}
