body:
[Lemma lem: bounds for integrals of hazard rate of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] For each $\varepsilon > 0$, there exist $K_\varepsilon \geq 0$ and compact sets $A_\varepsilon \subset B_\varepsilon \subset U_g$ such that $A_\varepsilon$ is inside the interior in $\mathbbm{R}_+^2$ of $B_\varepsilon$ and the following properties hold:
	\begin{equation*}
		\int_{A_\varepsilon} g(x, y)dxdy \geq 1 - \varepsilon \quad \text{and} \quad h_g^x(x, y) + h_g^y(x, y) \leq K_\varepsilon \quad \text{for all} \quad (x, y) \in B_\varepsilon.
	\end{equation*}
	Suppose that $\psi$ is continuous and $\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{(x, y) \in A_\varepsilon\right\}} \leq \psi(x, y) \leq \mathbbm{1}_{\left\{(x, y) \in B_\varepsilon\right\}}$ for all $x, y \in \mathbbm{R}_+$, then
	\begin{equation*}
		\max\left\{E\left|\bar\boldsymbol{D}_t^N((1 - \psi)\varphi)\right|, E\left|\bar\boldsymbol{D}_t^{N, c}((1 - \psi)\varphi)\right|\right\} \leq \varepsilon \left(\bar M + \frac{E\expectarg*{\mathcal{R}^N(t)}}{N}\right) \left|\left|\varphi\right|\right|_\infty.
	\end{equation*}
	for all $t \geq 0$ and $\varphi \in C_b(\mathbbm{R}_+^3)$. This inequality in fact holds if $0 \leq \psi \leq 1$ and $\psi = 1$ in~$A_\varepsilon$. In particular, the condition involving $B_\varepsilon$ is not needed to prove the inequality, but will be used when we invoke the lemma in the sequel.

