[Proposition 13 (CondSOC Gibbs identity) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] For a controlled law \(P^{z,\bm v}\) started at \(x_0\),
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v)
=\E_{P^{z,\bm v}}\left[
\frac12\int_0^T\norm{\bm v_t}^2\,\dd t
+\ell_{\varepsilon,y}(X_T)\right]
\end{equation*}
satisfies
\begin{equation}
\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v)+\log Z_{z,\varepsilon}
=\KL(P^{z,\bm v}\|Q^{z,\varepsilon}).
\end{equation}
If \(\bm v^{z,\varepsilon}\) is the Doob control of \(Q^{z,\varepsilon}\), then
\begin{equation}
\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v)-\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v^{z,\varepsilon})
=\frac12\E_{P^{z,\bm v}}\int_0^T
\norm{\bm v_t-\bm v_t^{z,\varepsilon}(X_t)}^2\,\dd t.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 18 (Weighted oscillatory ergodic averages) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Under the standing CPE hypothesis, let $q\in L^1(X,\mu)$ and
$w\in C_c^\infty(\bR^d;\bC)$. For
$\alpha\in\bT^d$, put
\begin{equation}

    B_R(\alpha;w,q)
    :=R^{-d}\sum_{k\in\bZ^d}
      w(k/R)e^{2\pi i\langle k,\alpha\rangle}U^kq.
\end{equation}
Then, in $L^1(X,\mu)$,
\begin{equation}

    B_R(\alpha;w,q)
    \longrightarrow
    \begin{cases}
      \displaystyle \left(\int_{\bR^d}w(x)\,dx\right)\E q,
          & \alpha=0,\\[6pt]
      0, & \alpha\neq0.
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}

