[Proposition thm:AuxApprox of arXiv:2606.01866, 'Phase Transition of a Semiflexible Membrane in Two Dimensions'] Fix $\lambda<0$, $d=2$, and let $G_N$ and $\bar{G}_N$ be as in (equation eq:cl of the paper) and (equation eq:ss of the paper), respectively. For a fixed $\delta\in(0,1)$ and $x,y\in V_N^\delta$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        |\bar{G}_N(x,y)-G^0_N(x,y)|=O(N^\lambda)
    \end{equation}
    and
    \begin{equation}
        |G_N(x,y)-\bar{G}_N(x,y)|=O(N^{\lambda-1})
    \end{equation}
    uniformly. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:two-edges of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] For the geometric inhomogeneous random graph  with $0\leq\gamma<\frac{1}{2}$ and either a hard profile and $\gamma\not=0$ or a soft profile with $\delta>2$ and with intensity \smash{$0< \lambda < \widehat{\lambda}_c$}, we have for all $\epsilon>0$, 
  \begin{align}
      \theta_{r, R} & \asymp \pi_{r, R}^{(2)}
      & \text{ on } \{  r \geq  R^\epsilon\},
       \\[2mm]
      \theta_{(u), R} & \asymp 
                 \pi_{(u), R}^{(2)} 
                 & \text{ on } \{u \leq R^{-\epsilon}\}.

  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

