[Prop HKKcor of arXiv:2605.10617, 'Logarithmic scaling of selective sweep curves:\\ from tents to houses'] Let $W^*:= W_{1/2}^*$ start in $0$. Then\\
a) for any $\beta > 0$
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{1\le n \le N^\beta} \big|\log_N W^*(n)-\log_N\sqrt n \, \big| \to 0 \quad \mbox{ a.s.\ as } N\to \infty,
\end{equation}
b) with $\tau_k$ as in~(equation deftauk of the paper),
\begin{equation}
   \max_{1\le k \le N} \max_{\tau_{k}(W^*)\le n < \tau_{k+1}(W^*)} \big(\log_N(k)- \log_N(W^*(n)\big) \to 0 \quad \mbox{ a.s.\ as } N\to \infty.
\end{equation}

[Lemme 72 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Given $\vsg\in \{\pm\}$ and $j \in \intn{1}{N-2}$, one has the upper bound

$$\om_j^{\vsg} \,= \,  \mathbbm{1}_{\{ \ups_j = -\vsg\}} \sum_{i=1}^j  \frac{|\lambda_{j+1}^{\vsg} - \lambda_{j+1}^{-\vsg} |}{\lambda_{j+1}^{-\vsg} - \lambda_{i}^{\vsg}}

+  \mathbbm{1}_{\{ \ups_{j+1}= -\vsg\}}

\sum_{i=j+2}^N \frac{|\lambda_{j+1}^{-\vsg} - \lambda_{j+1}^{\vsg}|}{\lambda_i^{\vsg} - \lambda_{j+1}^{-\vsg} }

\leq N+1 \, .$$

