[Lemma 19 (Quotient asymptotics) of arXiv:2608.30551, 'Critical Discrete Hardy Inequalities in $L^p$'] Let \(\sigma\in(0,1/2)\), \(\alpha\in(\sigma,1/2)\), and
\(a\in(0,1]\). Define \(\gamma\) by
\[
    1-2\gamma=a(1-2\alpha).
\]
Then \(\gamma\in(\sigma,1/2)\), and, as \(|x|\to\infty\),
\[
    \frac{\Delta^\sigma k_{-\alpha}^{a}(x)}
         {k_{-\alpha}^{a}(x)}
    =
    \frac{\mathcal A_{\gamma-\sigma}}{\mathcal A_\gamma}
    \frac{1}{|x|^{2\sigma}}
    +
    O\left(
        \frac{1}
        {|x|^{2\sigma+1-\max\{2\sigma,1-2\gamma\}}}
    \right).
\]

