[Definition of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $S\subset T$ be a cleft and let ${\mathcal{C}}_1,{\mathcal{C}}_2,{\mathcal{D}}$ be $S$-cocomplete $T$-$\infty$-categories. A functor ${\mathcal{C}}_1\times{\mathcal{C}}_2\to{\mathcal{D}}$ is called \emph{$S$-cocontinuous in each variable} or \emph{$S$-bilinear} if for every $A\in T$ and $X_1\in{\mathcal{C}}_1(A), X_2\in{\mathcal{C}}_2(A)$ the two composites
    \begin{align*}
        \{X_1\}\times\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_2&\lhook\joinrel\longrightarrow \pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_1\times\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_2\xrightarrow{\;\pi_A^*F\;}\pi_A^*{\mathcal{D}}\\
        \pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_1\times\{X_2\}&\lhook\joinrel\longrightarrow\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_1\times\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_2\xrightarrow{\;\pi_A^*F\;}\pi_A^*{\mathcal{D}}
    \end{align*}
    preserve $(T_{/A}\times_TS)$-colimits in the usual sense. Analogously, we define what it means for ${\mathcal{C}}_1\times\cdots\times{\mathcal{C}}_n\to{\mathcal{D}}$ to be $S$-cocontinuous in each variable (\emph{$S$-multilinear}).

[Lemma l:tau_analytics of arXiv:2603.28578, 'Exponential Bounds and Analyticity for the Tree Builder Random Walk'] Let $B_n \in \mathcal{F}_n$, then there exists $A_n \in \mathcal{F}_n$, such that
\begin{equation}
P_p(B_n, \tau_1 = n, H_o = \infty) = P_p(A_n)P_p(H_o = \infty)
\end{equation}
and that
\begin{equation}
P_p(A_n) \le P_p(\tau_1 \ge n).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition d:cdm of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] {\rm Let $\{V_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ be sets with $|V_n| \to \infty$. Fix an integer $d\geq 2$, as well as a real number $\alpha\in (0,d]$. We consider subsets $$ J_n\subseteq \underbrace{ \, V_n\times \cdots \times V_n \, }_\text{$d$ times}, \quad n\geq 1,$$ (each $J_n$ is not necessarily symmetric and has possibly diagonal components) and say that the sequence $\{J_n\}$ has \emph{combinatorial dimension} equal to $\alpha$ if there exist finite constants $0<c'\leq c$ such that the following two properties are verified for $n$ sufficiently large: 
\begin{itemize}
    \item for all $A_1,...,A_d\subseteq V_n$,
\begin{equation}
| J_n \cap (A_1\times \cdots \times A_d)| \leq c \, \max_{i=1,...,d} |A_i|^\alpha\,;
\end{equation}
\item moreover, 
\begin{equation}
| J_n | \geq c' \, |V_n |^\alpha\,, \quad n\geq 1.
\end{equation}

\end{itemize}
}

[Defn def:local of arXiv:2606.21049, '\textsc{Locality of rough path lifts}'] Let $\mathbb{A}$ be an area process on $P\subset C^\gamma \times C^\gamma$.
We will say that $\mathbb{A}$ is \emph{local} if for $Z, Z' \in P$ and any $(s,t) \in \triangle$, one has the implication
\begin{equation*}
Z_{s,[s,t]} = Z'_{s,[s,t]} \implies \mathbb{A}_{s,t}(Z) = \mathbb{A}_{s,t}(Z') \;.
\end{equation*}

[Theorem the: compensator of departures-driven process of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] For each $\varphi \in C_b(\mathbbm{R}_+^3)$, the process $\boldsymbol{D}(\varphi)$ has integrable total variation over finite intervals of time. Further, its compensator is the process $\boldsymbol{D}^c(\varphi)$ defined as:
	\begin{equation*}
		\boldsymbol{D}_t^c(\varphi) \vcentcolon= \int_0^t \angled{\varphi_s\left[r(\boldsymbol{\mu}_s)h_g^x + h_g^y\right]}{\boldsymbol{\mu}_s}ds \quad \text{for all} \quad t \geq 0.
	\end{equation*}

