[Proposition 47 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $(Y,Y'), (Z,Z') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W)$ and $f \in C_b^{2\alpha,3}([0,T] \times W, \bar{W})$ be arbitrary. Then we have
\begin{align*}
\interleave (f(Y),f(Y)')-(f(Z),f(Z)') \interleave_{X,2\alpha} &\leq C \big( 1 + | Y,Y' |_{X,2\alpha}^2 + | Z,Z' |_{X,2\alpha}^2 \big)
\\ &\quad \interleave (Y,Y') - (Z,Z') \interleave_{X,2\alpha},
\end{align*}
where the constant $C > 0$ depends on $\alpha$, $T$, $X$ and $\| f \|_{C_b^{2 \alpha,3}}$. Moreover, for $T \leq 1$ the constant $C$ does not depend on $T$.

