[Lemma eq:kernel_lower_bound of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:integrability}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 1$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel.

    Suppose that $J$ satisfies $J(x,y) = \Omega(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 0$.

    If $\alpha > 1$ then there exists $c = c(G,J) > 0$ such that     for all $x \in V$ and $r \in \mathbf{N}$

    \begin{equation}

        c
        r^{d(1-\alpha)}
        \leq
        \sum_{L = r}^{\infty}
        \sum_{y \in S(x,L)}
        J(x,y).
    \end{equation}

    If $\alpha \leq 1$ then $\sum_{L = r}^{\infty} \sum_{y \in S(x,L)} J(x,y) = \infty$ and hence $\sum_{L = r}^{\infty} \mathbf{E}_{\beta} \left[ \deg(x,L) \right] = \infty$ for all $x \in V$ and $r \in \mathbf{N}$.

    Suppose that $J$ satisfies $J(x,y) = O(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.

    Then there exists $c = c(G,J) > 0$ such that     for all $x \in V$ and $r \in \mathbf{N}$

    \begin{equation}

        \sum_{L = r}^{\infty}
        \sum_{y \in S(x,L)}
        J(x,y)
        \leq 
        c 
        r^{d(1-\alpha)}.
    \end{equation}

    In particular, $\sum_{y \in V \setminus \{x\}} J(x,y) < \infty$ and $\mathbf{E}_{\beta} \left[ \deg(x) \right] < \infty$ for all $x \in G$.

