[Definition 7 of arXiv:2609.00736, 'Modalities in non-classical variations of S4'] Let $M = \tuple{W, W^\bot, \preceq, \R, V}$ be a birelational $\csf$-model.
    Then, $M$ is:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item an \emph{$\isf$-model} iff it is forward and backward confluent;
        \item a \emph{$\gsf$-model} iff it is a locally linear $\isf$-model; and
        \item a \emph{$\gsfc$-model} iff it is a downward confluent $\gsf$-model.
    \end{itemize}

