{"artifact_digest":"sha256:27ebeaaf5a6f43a75eeb44e49200c17bbee00a92ea65646996694f7030bc8aab","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/27/27ebeaaf5a6f43a75eeb44e49200c17bbee00a92ea65646996694f7030bc8aab.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:9fc897373b66a14c7407af418096e5cc44adf40ba811f2ddc5341de03a994166","bundle_entry_key":"2605-02713-lemma-8-3-4","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_025","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_025.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-02713-lemma-8-3-4","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: As $ k^{-1/2} \big( 1 - \gamma / n^\beta \big)^{k} $ is monotone decreasing in $k$, the integral criterium leads to 
	\begin{align}
		\sum_{k=1}^n \frac{1}{\sqrt{k}}  \Big( 1 - \frac{\gamma}{n^\beta} \Big)^{k} \leq 1 - \frac{\gamma}{n^\beta} + \int_1^n \frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}  \Big( 1 - \frac{\gamma}{n^\beta} \Big)^x \mathrm{d}  x . 
	\end{align}
	If $\beta <1$, observe that $1-y \leq e^{-y}$ for $y \in [0,1]$ and substituting $z:= x \, (\gamma/n^\beta)$ leads to 
	$$
