body:
[Definition def:bracket of arXiv:2601.10359, 'An Operator It\^o Formula for Volterra Gaussian Processes:\\ The Intrinsic Bracket via Cau'] Let $Y = (Y_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ be such that $Y_t\in\Dom(D)$ for a.e.\ $t$ and $t\mapsto \Pi DY_t$ lies in $L^2([0,T]\times\Omega;\mathcal{H})$. Define the \emph{energy function}
\begin{equation}
\Gamma^Y(t) := \left\|\Pi DY_t\right\|_\mathcal{H}^2
\end{equation}
and the \emph{intrinsic bracket}
\begin{equation}
\langle Y\rangle^{(D,\Pi)}_t := \Gamma^Y(t) = \left\|\Pi DY_t\right\|_\mathcal{H}^2.
\end{equation}
For centered Gaussian processes, $\Gamma^Y(t) = \mathbb{E}[Y_t^2]$.

[Corollary Upper bound for cumulants of Wigner of arXiv:2411.11341, 'Ultra high order cumulants and quantitative CLT for polynomials in Random Matrices'] Let $\mathcal{X}\sim Wigner$. For any $r\geq 2$ and $m$ even, we have
\begin{equation}
|N^{r/2-1}K_r(\text{Tr}(Y_1),\dots,\text{Tr}(Y_r))|\leq B_m (2\mathsf{C})^mm!^2 |p(m)||p(m/2)| \prod_{k=1}^m ||D_{j_k}||,
\end{equation}
where $B_m$ is the $m^{th}$-Bell number and $p(n)$ is the set of integer partitions of $n$.

