[Theorem thm:TT-F of arXiv:2608.30166, 'Square Functions and Rectifiability\\ under Monotone Transformations of the Density'] Let $\mu$ be a Radon measure in $\mathbb{R}^d$ such that
$0<\Theta^n_*(x,\mu)\le\Theta^{n,*}(x,\mu)<\infty$ for $\mu$-a.e.\ $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$, and
let $F\colon(0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}$ be locally bi-Lipschitz. The following are equivalent:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] $\mu$ is $n$-rectifiable.
\item[(b)] $\displaystyle\int_0^1|\Delta^F_\mu(x,r)|^2\,\frac{dr}{r}<\infty$ for
$\mu$-a.e.\ $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$.
\item[(c)] $\displaystyle\lim_{r\to0}\Delta^F_\mu(x,r)=0$ for $\mu$-a.e.\ $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$.
\end{itemize}

[Lemma 5 (Tail Bound on the Leakage Probability) of arXiv:2608.28198, 'Performative Privacy: When Differential Privacy Maximizes Utility'] Let $Z_{t}$ be the dataset at the beginning of round $t$ and $z \in Z_{t}$ be a target record. Let $o_t \sim \mathcal{M}(Z_{t})$ be the candidate output. Define the factual and counterfactual output distributions as $P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{in}}(\cdot) = \Pr[\mathcal{M}(Z_{t}) = \cdot \mid z \in Z_{t}]$ and $P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{out}}(\cdot) = \Pr[\mathcal{M}(Z_{t} \setminus \{z\}) = \cdot]$. 

For the log-likelihood ratio $\Lambda(o_t|z) = \ln \left( \frac{P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{in}}(o_t)}{P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{out}}(o_t)} \right)$ evaluated at output $o_t$, and for any threshold $\tau > 0$ and order $\alpha > 1$, the tail probability of leakage is bounded by:
\begin{align*}
\Pr_{o_t \sim P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{in}}}(\Lambda(o_t|z) > \tau) \le \exp \Big( -(\alpha - 1) \big( \tau - D_\alpha(P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{in}} \parallel P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{out}}) \big) \Big) 
\end{align*}
where $D_\alpha(P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{in}} \parallel P^{\mathcal{M}}_{\text{out}})$ is the Rényi divergence of order $\alpha$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

