[Lemma lem.decom_DF of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Let $v_{m}$ defined in (equation eq.harmonicBC of the paper) follow the canonical grain extension (equation eq.def_extension_plan of the paper) on ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m$, then for every $F \subseteq E_d({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m)$ we have
		\begin{equation}
			\forall x \in {\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m, \qquad (D_F v_m)(x) = (\nabla_{F_\circ} D_{F_*} v_m)(x).
		\end{equation}
		Here $F_*, F_\circ$ follows the decomposition (equation eq.def_WIP_new of the paper).

