[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.02319, 'Averaging Principle for Ordinary Differential Equations in a Multiscale Random Environment'] Let $n\geq1$ and $z\in\mathbb R^d$, then for all $0<t<T$, if \eqref{hyp:Fbound} and \eqref{hyp:Lip} are satisfied we have
\begin{align*}
\lvert\mathbf Z_t^{n,z}\rvert\leq\big(\lvert z\rvert+T\,M_T^n)\,e^{TL_T^n},
\end{align*}
where for all $t>0$ and $n\geq1$
\begin{align*}
M_t^n:=\sup_{s\in[0,t]}M_{\mathbf I_s^n}.
\end{align*}

