[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] For a non-negative function $w \in C_{0}(\bR^{d})$ with $w \not\equiv 0$,
  let $\nu = -\theta_{c} \mu + w \cdot dx$. Then the ground state $h$ satisfies
  \begin{align}

    h(x) = \int_{\bR^{d}}^{ } G^{\nu}(x,y) h(y) w(y) dy, \quad \text{for all $x \in \mathbb{R}^{d}$}.
  \end{align}

