[Definition def:sum of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Let $\mu_A$ and $\mu_B$ be exponentially decaying measures on $W_N$. Define $\mu_C:= \mu_A \boxplus_{N}^{\beta} \mu_B$ (also written as $C=A\boxplus_{N}^{\beta}B$) to be the measure whose Bessel generating function is given by
\begin{equation}
G_N (x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta,\mu_C) = G_N(x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta,\mu_A)G_N(x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta,\mu_B).
\end{equation}

