[Lemma lemma-5.2 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] Suppose that~$f\colon\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$ admits the Fourier representation
\begin{equation}

f(z) = \sum_{q\in\mathbb Z}w(q)\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{2\pi\text{\rm  i}\mkern0.7mu q z}
\end{equation}
such that $\{w(q)\}_{q\in\mathbb Z}\in\ell^1(\mathbb Z)$. Then for all $\alpha\in\mathbb R$,
\begin{equation}

E\bigl(\,\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{2\pi\text{\rm  i}\mkern0.7mu\alpha\phi_0}f(\phi_0)\,\big|\,\mathcal F_1\bigr) = \text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{v_0(\phi_1)+2\pi\text{\rm  i}\mkern0.7mu\alpha\phi_1}
\sqrt{\frac{2\pi\sigma_0^2}\beta}
\sum_{q\in\mathbb Z} w\ast a(q)\,\theta_0^{(q+\alpha)^2}\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{2\pi\text{\rm  i}\mkern0.7mu q\phi_1},
\end{equation}
where~$\{a(q)\}_{q\in\mathbb Z}$ are the Fourier coefficients of~$\nu$; i.e., $a(q):=\int_{[0,1)}\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{- 2\pi\text{\rm  i}\mkern0.7mu qz}\nu(\text{\rm d}\mkern0.5mu z)$, and $w\ast a$ is the usual convolution,
\begin{equation}

w\ast a(q):=\sum_{\ell\in\mathbb Z} w(q-\ell)a(\ell),\quad q\in\mathbb Z.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition DEF:WEAK of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] We say that {weak synchronization} holds if there exists a random point \(b: \tilde{\mathcal{B}} \to \mathbb{R}^d\) such that for \(\mathbf{P}\)-almost every \(\omega^- \in \tilde{\mathcal{B}}\),
	\begin{align*}
		\mathrm{supp}(\mu_{\omega^-}) = \{ b(\omega^-) \}.
	\end{align*}

[Definition 28 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] We endow the space $\scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T], \bar{W})$ with the seminorm
\begin{align}
\| Y,Y' \|_{X,2\alpha} := \| Y' \|_{\alpha} + \| R^Y \|_{2 \alpha}.
\end{align}

