body:
[Corollary cor:strong_recovery of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Suppose that the conditions of Theorem (theo:tied-SGD of the paper) and
Assumption (assum:effective_pl of the paper) hold. Let $n_0:=\left\lceil\frac{T_0d}{4\alpha_d}\right\rceil$. Then, for every fixed target accuracy \(\epsilon>0\), there exists
\begin{equation}
n_\epsilon=n_0+O\left(\frac{d}{\alpha_d}\log_+\frac1\epsilon\right),

\end{equation}
such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{d\to\infty}\mathbb P\left(\Psi_d(W^{(n_\epsilon)})-\Psi^*>\epsilon\right)=0.

\end{equation}
where $\log_+(x):=\max\{0,\log x\}$.
In particular, if \(T_0=\Theta(1)\), reaching an \(\epsilon\)-suboptimal population loss requires at most $O\left(\frac{d}{\alpha_d}\log\frac1\epsilon\right)$ additional samples.

