[Definition 13 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] Let $(x_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a stationary process and $S_x(\omega)$ be its SD. If $S_x$ is bounded and satisfies $S_x(\omega)\xrightarrow{\omega\to\pm\I}0$, we define 
    \begin{align}
        S_x^{\max}:= \max\limits_{\omega\in\R}S_x(\omega).
    \end{align}

[Theorem 25 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] Let $p=(4a-1)/4a$ and $\{Z_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ be uniformly bounded. Then, we have the following law of iterated logarithm for $\{W_n\}_{n\ge1}$:
\begin{equation*}
\limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{W_n}{\sqrt{2n\log n\log \log\log n}}=\mu (2a-1)\ \ \text{a.s.}
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:bddness of arXiv:2511.12692, 'A stochastic flow approach to De Giorgi--Nash--Moser estimates for SPDE\lowercase{s} with '] In addition to the assumptions of Proposition (prop:Existence_Uniqueness of the paper), we assume that a.s. $u_0\in L^\infty(\mathbb{T}^d)$,
		\begin{equation}
	f^0\in L^{p/2}(0,\tau;L^{q/2}(\mathbb{T}^d)),\quad \text{ and }\quad
	f^1, \ldots, f^d\in L^p(0,\tau;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))
    \ \ \text{and} \ \  g\in L^p(0,\tau;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d;\ell^2)),\end{equation}
	for some $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ with $\frac{2}{p}+\frac{d}{q}<1$ and let $u$ be the solution to (equation eq:SPDE_lin of the paper). Then,  a.s., $u\in L^\infty([0,\tau]\times \mathbb{T}^d)$, and we have the estimate
    \begin{align}
        {\mathbb E}\|u\|_{L^\infty([0,\tau]\times \mathbb{T}^d)}^r \,\le \, C
        {\mathbb E}\biggl[
        \|u_0\|_{L^\infty(\mathbb{T}^d)}^r + \|f^0 \|_{L^{p/2}(0,\tau;L^{q/2}(\mathbb{T}^d))}^r + \sum_{i=1}^d
        \|f^i\|_{ L^p(0,\tau;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^r +\| g \|_{L^p(0,\tau;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d;\ell^2))}^r
        \biggr]
    \end{align}
    for any $r>0$, where $C$ depends only on $(d,T,M,\nu, p,q,r)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

