body:
[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2609.02175, '2609.02175'] Let $g_1$ and $g_2$ be smooth Riemannian metrics on
	$\mathbb R^n$, $n\geq3$. Assume that there exists $R>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\operatorname{supp}(g_j-g_0)
		\Subset B(0,R),
		\qquad j=1,2,
	\end{equation}
	and that $(B(0,R),g_j)$ is simple for $j=1,2$.
	Assume moreover that $(B(0,R),g_1)$ satisfies one of the
	following conditions:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item the sectional curvature is non-positive;
		\item there are no focal points;
		\item the sectional curvature is non-negative.
	\end{enumerate}
	If
	\begin{equation}
		\|S_{g_1,h}(\lambda)-S_{g_2,h}(\lambda)\|
		_{\mathcal B(L^2(\mathbb S^{n-1}))}
		=
		o(1),
		\qquad h\to0,
	\end{equation}
	then there exists a diffeomorphism
	\begin{equation}
		\psi:B(0,R)\longrightarrow B(0,R),
		\qquad
		\psi|_{\partial B(0,R)}
		=
		\operatorname{Id},
	\end{equation}
	such that
	\begin{equation}
		g_1
		=
		\psi^*g_2.
	\end{equation}

