body:
[Proposition B4re of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $R_{n-1,N}(s)$ and $R_{n,N-1}(s)$ be the integral remainders defined in (equation B4D of the paper). For $s\in\left[s_0,N^{\frac{1}{6}}\right]$, we have
\begin{equation*}
    N^{\frac{2}{3}}R_{n-1,N}(s),~N^\frac{2}{3}R_{n,N-1}(s)\le C(s_0,\gamma)e^{-\frac{s}{2}}
\end{equation*}
when $N$ is large for some constant $C(s_0,\gamma)$.

