[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Under assumptions \textbf{H1}--\textbf{H3} and \textbf{A4}. As \(\epsilon\to 0\), \(x^\epsilon\) weakly converges to \(\bar x\), that is 
\begin{equation}
\dd \bar z_t = D\bar g(\bar x_t) \bar z_t \dd t+Df(\bar x_t) \bar z_t \dd B^H_t+ \bar V^{\frac{1}{2}}(\bar x_t)\dd \hat W_t,\ \bar x_0 = x,
\end{equation}
where \(\bar x\) satisfies the ODE \eqref{averaged-system}, and \(V(x,y):=(D_y \Phi \sigma)(D_y \Phi \sigma)^{*}(x,y)\) with $\bar V^{\frac{1}{2}}(x)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{m}} V^{\frac{1}{2}}(x,y)\mu^{x}(dy)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 4 (Integrated slow variation) of arXiv:2608.01674, '\textbf{Limit Theorems for Tempered Linear Processes with Innovations in the Domain of Att'] Under \cref{ass:filter}, $L$ is slowly varying,
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\ell(x)}{L(x)}\longrightarrow0, ~~~~\text{as} ~~x\to\infty,

\end{equation}
and, for every $c>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \frac{L(cx)-L(x)}{\ell(x)}\longrightarrow\log c.

\end{equation}
More generally, if $0<a<b<\infty$ and $f$ is continuous on $[a,b]$,
then as $N\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \frac1{\ell(N)}
 \sum_{aN<j\le bN}\frac{\ell(j)}{j}f(j/N)
 \longrightarrow
 \int_a^b\frac{f(u)}{u}\dd u.

\end{equation}
The same conclusion holds with $a=0$ whenever
$f(u)=O(u^\rho)$ as $u\downarrow0$ for some $\rho>0$.

[Cor 3 (Corollary \ref{Cor psi Vandermonde}) of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $n\geq 1$
and let $\alpha_{n}>\alpha_{n-1}>\dots >\alpha_{1}>\alpha_{0}=1$.
Let $(c_{0}, c_{1}, \dots, c_{n})$
be the unique solution to the linear system
\begin{displaymath}
\forall k\in \{0,\dots, n-1\},
\sum_{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \alpha_{i}^{-(k+1/2)} = 0,
\qquad
\sum_{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \alpha_{i}^{-(n+1/2)} = 1.
\end{displaymath}
Then
\begin{displaymath}
\psi_{2n+1, A} = \lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} (-1)^{n}\dfrac{2^{n} n! (n+1/2)}{(2\pi)^{n}}\vert\log\varepsilon\vert^{n+1/2}
\sum_{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \ind_{\Ns_{\varepsilon^{\alpha_{i}}}(A)},
\end{displaymath}
with convergence in $L^{2}(d\PP,\sigma(\Phi),H^{-\eta}(\C))$ for $\eta>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:h-collected-chernoff of arXiv:2602.21315, 'The Instability of all Backoff Protocols\thanks{For the purpose of Open Access, the author'] Let $\alpha > 0$, and let $j\ge1$ be a sufficiently large integer. Let $Y$ be a sum of independent Bernoulli random variables with mean $\mu$. If $\mu \leq \alpha^2 j(\log j)^2/6$, then with probability at least $1-j^{-3j}$, 
\begin{equation}
    Y \le \alpha^2 j(\log j)^2.
    \end{equation}
    Otherwise, with probability at least $1-j^{-3j}$,
    \begin{equation}
        Y \le \Big(1 + \frac{\alpha j^{1/2}\log j}{4\mu^{1/2}}\Big)\mu < 2\mu.
    \end{equation}

