[Definition eqn:dim-res-2 of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] Suppose $\mathcal M, \mathcal M'$ are instanton $SO(3)$-flow categories. An \textit{instanton $SO(3)$-bimodule} $W: \mathcal M \to \mathcal M'$ of degree $d$ consists of the following data. For each $\alpha \in \mathsf{orb}(\mathcal M)$ and $\alpha' \in \mathsf{orb}(\mathcal M')$ with \begin{equation}|\alpha| - |\alpha'| + d \le \dim \mathscr O(\alpha') + 1,\end{equation} 
there is a compact stratified-smooth $SO(3)$-manifold of dimension $|\alpha| - |\alpha'| + \dim \mathscr O(\alpha)+ d$, denoted $\mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W;\alpha, \alpha')$. As in the case of flow categories, we demand that each element of $\mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \alpha, \alpha')$ has stabilizer conjugate to one of $\{I\}, SO(2)$, or $SO(3)$. This manifold is equipped with equivariant maps 
\[\mathscr O(\alpha) \xleftarrow{s_{\alpha\alpha'}} \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W;\alpha, \alpha') \xrightarrow{t_{\alpha\alpha'}} \mathscr O(\alpha')\]
called the source and target maps. Whenever $\alpha, \alpha'$ satisfy (equation eqn:dim-res-2 of the paper), there are equivariant composition maps 
\begin{align*}
\circ: \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(\alpha, \beta) \times_{\beta} \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \beta, \alpha') &\to \partial\mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \alpha, \alpha') \\
\circ: \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \alpha, \beta') \times_{\beta'} \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(\beta', \alpha') &\to \partial\mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \alpha, \alpha')
\end{align*}
which are compatible with the source and target maps, and associate with the composition maps of $\mathcal M$ and $\mathcal M'$. We also require that these induce a diffeomorphism 
\begin{align}
\partial \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \alpha, \alpha') \cong &\bigsqcup_{\substack{\beta \in \mathsf{orb}(\mathcal M)}} \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(\alpha, \beta) \times_{\beta} \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \beta, \alpha') \\
&\bigsqcup_{\substack{\beta' \in \mathsf{orb}(\mathcal M')}} \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W;\alpha, \beta') \times_{\beta'} \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(\beta', \alpha').
\end{align}
Finally, there is an equivariant diffeomorphism $U: \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; \alpha, \alpha') \to \mkern3mu\widetilde{\mkern-3muM\mkern-1mu}\mkern1mu(W; U\alpha, U\alpha')$ which is compatible with the source, target, and composition maps defined above.

