[Lem ideal of arXiv:2411.09640, 'Random Lipschitz functions on graphs with weak expansion'] There is a constant $C$ for which the following holds. For any $\gamma>C$, if $k>\gamma M^2\log(Mn)$, then for $\mathbf{f}$ chosen uniformly at random from $\mbox{\rm{Lip}}_{v_0}(C_{n,k}; M)$, for any $v \in V$,
\begin{equation}\label{nonideal}
\mathbb{P}(|\bar\mathbf{f}_{N_v^+}| \ne M+1) = O((\gamma n)^{-1}).
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $\log M=o_n(\log n)$, then
\begin{equation}\label{nonideal'}
\mathbb{P}(|\bar\mathbf{f}_{N_v^+}| \ne M+1) = o_n(n^{-1}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorema them:critere_id_intro of arXiv:2412.10001, 'On the Markov transformation of Gaussian processes'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t \in \mathbb{R}}$ be a Gaussian process with continuous covariance function $K : (s,t) \mapsto \mathbb{E}((X_s-\mathbb{E}(X_s))(X_t- \mathbb{E}(X_t)))$ and $\alpha^K : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}_+$ that satisfies, for every $s<t \in \mathbb{R}^2$,
			\begin{equation}
				\sup_{(v,h) \in [s,t] \times ]0,h^*]} \left|\alpha^K(v)- \frac{1}{h}\left(1 - \frac{K(v,v+h)}{\sqrt{K(v,v)}\sqrt{K(v+h,v+h)}} \right) \right| \xrightarrow[h^* \to 0^+]{} 0.
			\end{equation} 
			Then, any Gaussian process $(Y_t)_{t \in \mathbb{R}}$ that satisfies, for every $s<t \in \mathbb{R}^2$, 
			\begin{equation}
				\mathbb{E}(Y_t) = \mathbb{E}(X_t) 
			\end{equation}
			and
			\begin{equation}
				\mathbb{E}((Y_s-\mathbb{E}(Y_s))(Y_t-\mathbb{E}(Y_t))) = \sqrt{K(s,s)}\sqrt{K(t,t)} \exp\left(-\int_s^t \alpha^K(u) du \right),
			\end{equation}is a strong local Markov transform of $X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

