[Lemma lem-Claim 5.2 of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] Let us assume that $z\in \mathrm{D}([0,T];U^\prime )$, $\alpha>0$
and $A \in \mathscr{A}_{2}(\alpha)$.
Let $(a_k)_{k\ge 2}$ be a sequence of functions {satisfying assumptions of Lemma (lem-Claim 5.1 of the paper).}

Then for every pair $(s,t)\in [0,T]^2_{+}$, the following convergence holds
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{s< r\le t} a_k(\Delta z(r)) \to \sum_{ s< r\le t} \1_A(\Delta z(r)).
\end{equation}

[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2506.11799, 'Quenched limit for diffusive biased random walks in random environment'] There exists an absolute constant $\rho>0$ such that, uniformly over all $U_1, U_2 \in \mathbb{V}_d$ we have that, 	for all $p \in (0, 2]$
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{E}_{U_1, U_2}\left[ (\tau_{1}^{(1)})^p \, \big| \, \mathcal{D}^\bullet = \infty \right] \le \rho \mathbb{E}_{U_1}\left[ \tau_{1}^p \, \big| \, D^{v^*} = \infty \right].
	\end{equation*}

