[Lemma lemma-6.7a of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] Given~$\widetilde\alpha\in(0,1)$, suppose~$\beta>0$ is such that $b\theta^2<b-1$ and $(b-1+\widetilde\alpha)\theta<1$. Under Assumption~(ass-1 of the paper), for each~$\boldsymbol\lambda_{0}\in\Sigma'$ there exists~$k_1\ge0$ such that
\begin{equation}

\sup_{q\ge0}\frac{\lambda_k(q+1)}{\lambda_k(q)}\le A_2\sqrt{b\theta-1}
\end{equation}
holds with
\begin{equation}

A_2:= \frac1{\widetilde\alpha}\sqrt{\frac1{1-(b-1)\theta}}
\end{equation}
for all~$k\ge0$ satisfying $\min\{k,n-k\}\ge k_1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

