[Define 8 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Another countably sub-additive capacity generated by $\mbE$ can be defined as follows:
 \begin{equation} \tildeCapc(A)=\inf\Big\{\lim_{n\to\infty}\mbE[\sum_{i=1}^n g_i]: I_A\le \sum_{n=1}^{\infty}g_n, 0\le g_n\in\mathcal{H}\Big\},\;\;\; A\in\mathcal F.
