[Prop rieszLaplaceLogFallback of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Assume $0\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2$, $\mu\in L^\infty\cap\mathcal{P}({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})$, and $\beta>0$ is fixed.  If $\mathsf{s}=0$, assume in addition (equation eq:logEnergyAssumption of the paper) and (equation eq:logRateExtraAssumptions of the paper).  Then there are constants $C_{\beta,\mu}<\infty$ and, in the case $\mathsf{s}=0$, $c_{\beta,\mu}>0$ such that, for all $N\ge1$,
\begin{align}
\Big|{\mathbb{E}}_{\mu^{\otimes N}}\Big[e^{-\frac{\beta}{2}W_N}\Big]
-\mathrm{det}_2(\mathrm{Id}+\beta T_\mu)^{-1/2}\Big|
\le C_{\beta,\mu}
\begin{cases}
(\log(e+N))^{-\frac{\mathsf{d}-2\mathsf{s}}{2\mathsf{s}}}, & 0<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2,\\[0.4em]
(e+N)^{-c_{\beta,\mu}}, & \mathsf{s}=0.
\end{cases}
\end{align}

