[Lemma 14 (Exact endpoint
decomposition) of arXiv:2608.06591, 'Random Triangles on Concentric Circles'] \protect\hypertarget{lem-endpoint}{}

Fix \(\delta > 0\) and let \[
J(\mu, \eta) = \int_0^{\delta}
  \left(x - \sqrt{\left[\mu x^2 - \eta\right]^{+}}\right) dx .
\] Then for \(\lvert\eta\rvert < \mu\delta^2\),
\begin{equation}\phantomsection{
J(\mu, \eta) = \frac{\eta}{4\sqrt{\mu}}\log\frac{1}{\lvert\eta\rvert}
  + A(\mu, \eta) ,
}\end{equation} where \(A\) is real analytic on a neighborhood of
\((1, 0)\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 13 (Low-energy reduced-kernel bound) of arXiv:2609.01436, '2609.01436'] Under \cref{ass:CL}, for
$0\leq x<y\leq z\leq\varepsilon\leq1/16$,
\begin{equation}
 W(x,y,z)\geq\frac{b_0}{2}\varepsilon^{\eta-1}.
\end{equation}

