[Theorem of arXiv:2609.03959, 'The combinatorial Hopf algebra of signed graphs'] Let $\Sigma$ be a signed graph then
\begin{equation}
\omega(X_{\Sigma}^\parallel(x_1,x_2,...)) = \sum_{\substack{(\kappa, \tau)}}x_{|\kappa(v_1)|}\cdots x_{|\kappa(v_d)|}
\end{equation}
where the sum runs over the pairs $(\kappa, \tau)$ where $\tau$ is an acyclic orientation of $\Sigma$ and $\kappa$ is a coloring compatible with $\tau$.

