[Lemma of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{prop:cluster_size_connectivity}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = O(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ for $\alpha > 1$. 

    For $k \in \mathbf{N}$, $b \in \mathbf{N}$, and $\mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b,k)$, there exists $c = c(G) > 0$ such that

    \begin{equation}
        \frac{1}{(b-1)!}
        \sum_{\mathbf{B} \in \mathcal{A}(b,\mathbf{m})}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            \mathcal{H}(\mathbf{B}) \text{ is connected}
        \right)
        \leq
        \prod_{i = 0}^{b-1}
        \left(
            c 
            \mathbf{E}_{\beta,J^{\star}}
            \left[
                \mathrm{length}(o)
            \right]
        \right)^{m_i}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma l:intermediate_estimate_pressure_deterministic of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (t:caccioppoli of the paper), for all $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and $\beta\in (\alpha,1]$, it holds that, a.e.\ on $\beta I\times \Omega$, 
\begin{align}

\| \pi\|_{L^{2}(\alpha B)}
\leq C_0 \|F\|_{L^2(\beta  B)}
+ C_0\|(\nabla \widetilde{\pi}_n)_n\|_{L^2(\beta  B;\ell^2)} +C_0 \|\pi\|_{H^{-1}(\beta B)},
\end{align} 
where $C_0$ depends only on $d,M,\varrho,\nu,\nu_0,r,\alpha$ and $\beta$.

