[Lemma lem:gauge-sym of arXiv:2608.01253, 'The pseudo-quantum representation of \\finite reversible Markov chains'] $P$ is reversible with respect to $\nu$ if and only if $A=DPD^{-1}$ is symmetric.
When it holds,

\begin{equation}
A=DPD^{-1}=D^{-1}P^{T}D,\qquad A^{T}=A.

\end{equation}

