[Proposition proposition_RN_time of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $t \geq 0$. The Radon-Nikodym derivative of ${\mathbb{P}}_{h}^{(\Omega,a,b)}$ with respect to ${\mathbb{P}}_{\operatorname{SLE}_3}^{(\Omega,a,b)}$ restricted to the $\sigma$-field $\sigma(\gamma(s): 0 \leq s \leq t)$ is given by
    \begin{equation} 
       \left. \frac{{\operatorname{d}} {\mathbb{P}}_{h}^{(\Omega,a,b)}}{{\operatorname{d}} {\mathbb{P}}_{\operatorname{SLE}_3}^{(\Omega,a,b)}}(\gamma)\right|_{ \sigma(\gamma(s): 0 \leq s \leq t)} =\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_h(\Omega)}\sum_{k \geq 0}\frac{h^k}{k!}\int_{\Omega_t^k}f_{t}^{(\pm,k)}(z_1,\dots,z_k) \prod_{j=1}^k dz_j
    \end{equation}
    where we have set $\Omega_t:= \Omega \setminus \gamma([0,t])$ and the functions $f_{t}^{(\pm,k)}:= f_{\Omega_t}^{(\pm,k)}$ are as in Theorem (theorem_spin_correlations of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

