[Prop uniformBoundRepulsive of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Assume $0\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2$, $\mu\in L^\infty\cap\mathcal{P}({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})$, and $\beta\ge0$ is fixed.  If $\mathsf{s}=0$, assume in addition (equation eq:logEnergyAssumption of the paper).  Then
\begin{align}
\sup_{N\ge1}{\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)\le C_{\mathrm{ub}}(\beta,\mu)<\infty.
\end{align}
If moreover, in the case $\mathsf{s}=0$, $\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d}}e^{-2\beta h_\mu}\,\mathop{}\!\mathrm d\mu<\infty$, then also
\begin{align}
\sup_{N\ge1}\ \sup_{0\le\eta\le\eta_0}\ {\mathbb{E}}_{\mu^{\otimes N}}\brak*{e^{-\frac{\beta}{2}W_{N,\eta}}}\le C_{\mathrm{cf}}(\beta,\mu)<\infty.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

