[Theorem thm:intro of arXiv:2412.05239, 'Conditions for uniform in time convergence: applications to averaging, numerical discretis'] Suppose the \textbf{General assumptions 1} hold. Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $\mathbb{X}$. Then there exists a constant $\tilde{\mathbf{C}}>0$, independent of $\delta$ and $t$, such that for all $t\ge 0$,
\begin{align} 
    \mathbf{dist} (\nu p_t, \nu p_t^{\delta}) \le \tilde{\mathbf{C}}\delta^{\alpha}.
\end{align}

