[Lemma lemma_Delta of arXiv:2603.29442, 'A compact support property for infinite-dimensional SDEs with Hölder continuous coefficien'] Suppose Assumption~(assumption1 of the paper) holds and that $X = (X_t)_{t\geq0}$ is a continuous $\ell^1_+$-valued solution to (equation e_sdesystem of the paper). For $i \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $\delta >0$, there exists a filtered probability space $(\Omega,\mathscr{F},(\mathscr{F}_t)_{t\geq 0},\mathbb{P})$ supporting a copy of $X$ and an $(\mathscr{F}_t)$-adapted pair $(W,\Delta) = ((W_t,\Delta_t))_{t \geq 0}$, where $W$ is an independent Brownian motion and $\Delta$ is a non-negative solution to

		\begin{equation} 
		d\Delta_t = (\delta - d_t(i))_+ dt + \Delta_t^\gamma dW_t
	\end{equation}

with $\Delta_0 = 0$.

