[Corollary 31 of arXiv:2608.20613, 'Random walks on wreath products \\and spectral gaps for coloured interchange processes'] Let $a_n(G)$ be the number of $\Sn_n$-spherical irreducible representations of $W_n(G)$, and let $f_n(G)$ be the number of these representations self-dual.  Then every minimal gap-determining family for $W_n(G)$ has cardinality $(a_n(G)+f_n(G))/2$.  Moreover,
\begin{align}
a_n(G)
&=[t^n]
\prod_{\gamma\in\Gamma}
\prod_{j=1}^{d_\gamma}\frac{1}{1-t^j},
\\
f_n(G)
&=[t^n]
\prod_{\substack{\gamma\in\Gamma\\\gamma\cong\gamma^*}}
\prod_{j=1}^{d_\gamma}\frac{1}{1-t^j}
\prod_{\{\gamma,\gamma^*\}:\,\gamma\not\cong\gamma^*}
\prod_{j=1}^{d_\gamma}\frac{1}{1-t^{2j}}.

\end{align}
In the second product of \eqref{eq:general-fixed-count}, each unordered dual pair is taken once. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:GeneralDiscrepancy of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Assume that $A_1,\ldots,A_n$ is a sequence of independent centered $m \times m$ random symmetric matrices, for some $m = m(n)$, that have $\|A_i\|_{\psi_1} \leq \psi$ for all $i \in [n]$ and satisfy Condition~(equation eq:NormConcentration of the paper). Then, there exist constants $C_1,C_2 > 0$ such that for $n \ll m^2$,
        \begin{equation*}
            \lim_{n \to \infty} \P{C_1\sqrt{nm} \leq \disc(A_1,\ldots,A_n) \leq C_2m^{3/2}} = 1.
        \end{equation*}
        In particular, when $n = \Theta(m^2)$, we have that $\disc(A_1,\ldots,A_n) = \Theta(m^{3/2})$ with high probability as $n \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem-explengthbrige of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] For any $M\in(0,\infty)$, there is a constant $C_M\in(0,\infty)$ (depending on $d$, $\beta$ and $M$) such that, for any $R\in\mathbb{N}$,
\begin{equation}
\sum_{n\in\mathbb{N}}n p_{y,x}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({W'}})}}}(n)\leq C_M |x-y|,\qquad y\in W',x\in (W')^{\rm c}.
\end{equation}

