[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Let $\mu$ be rational. For any $\epsilon>0$, we have 
\begin{align*}
&\limsup_{\cI_{\mu}\ni N\to \infty} 
\frac{1}{N} \log \sN(\cC_{N,\mu}, \sqrt{N}\epsilon) 
\le R_{\mu}\left(\frac{\epsilon^2}{16}\right)\\
&\liminf_{\cI_{\mu}\ni N\to \infty} 
\frac{1}{N} \log \sN(\cC_{N,\mu}, \sqrt{N}\epsilon)
\ge R_\mu(\epsilon^2).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 13 (Pathwise Sobolev space $\mathcal{W}^{2, \pi}_{\omega}$) of arXiv:2608.07365, 'A pathwise Ito formula \\for weakly differentiable functions'] Define   $\mathcal{W}^{2, \pi}_{\omega}$ to be the space of functions $F\in W^{2,1}(\Rr^d)$ for which there exists a sequence $(F_m)_{m\geq 1}$ such that
\eq{
  F_m\in C^2_b(\Rr^d)\cap W^{2, 1}(\Rr^d)\qquad \qquad  \nonumber\\
F_m(\omega(t)) \to F(\omega(t)),\, \forall t\in [0, T],\quad
\|\nabla^2 F_m -\nabla^2 F\|_{\mathcal{W}^{0}_{\omega, \pi}}\xrightarrow{m\to \infty} 0.
}
\eq{
\mathcal{W}^{2}_{\omega, \pi}:=\Big\{F\in W^{2,1}(\Rr^d)\colon\, \exists (F_m)_{m\geq 1}\  \text{\rm satisfying } \eqref{2eq:W2pomega}\Big\}.
}

