[Definition def:Pisztora_event of arXiv:2603.28520, 'The Supercritical Loop O(1) and Random Current Models: Uniqueness and Mixing'] For a box $\Lambda_n$ (or a translate of it), Pisztora considered the event $\mathtt{Pis}_{\Lambda_n}(\varepsilon, \theta, L_0)$ defined as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[$i)$] There is a cluster $\mathtt{Giant}_{\Lambda_n} $ touching all faces of $\partial_v \Lambda_n$ and the box $\Lambda_{n/2}$. 
    \item[$ii)$] The cluster has a density: $\abs{\mathtt{Giant}_{\Lambda_n}}\geq (\theta- \varepsilon)|\Lambda_n|$.
    \item[$iii)$] Most other clusters have size bounded by $L_0:$ $\abs{ \left \{v \in \Lambda_n \setminus \mathtt{Giant}_{\Lambda_n} \mid \abs{\mathcal{C}_v} \geq L_0 \right \} } \leq \varepsilon |\Lambda_n|.$
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] Let $\eps_i\to0$ and suppose
\begin{equation}
  \norm{\phi_i}_{C^0_\delta}=1,
  \qquad
  \eps_i^\delta
  \norm{\widetilde{\mathcal P}_{\eps_i}\phi_i}_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\delta-4}}
  \longrightarrow0.
\end{equation}
If $\phi_i\to u$ locally on $X\setminus S$, then $u=0$.

