[Defn Free state of i.i.d-increments of arXiv:2411.13465, 'Height-offset variables and pinning at infinity for gradient Gibbs measures on trees'] Given a positive symmetric transfer operator $Q \in \ell^\frac{d+1}{2}(\mathbb{Z})$, we call the probability measure $\nu$ on $(\Omega^\nabla, \mathcal{F}^\nabla)$ with marginals     
\begin{equation}
		\nu(\eta_{\Lambda \cup \partial \Lambda}=\zeta_{\Lambda \cup \partial \Lambda})=\frac{1}{Z_\Lambda}\prod_{(x,y) \in {}^\rho\Vec{E}_{\Lambda \cup \partial \Lambda}}Q(\zeta_{(x,y)}).
	\end{equation}
 \textbf{the free state (of i.i.d.-increments)}.

[Theorem thm:gram of arXiv:2609.01672, '\textbf{All-Minors Matrix-Tree Theory for Superport Networks:\\ Completed Quotient-Inciden'] Let \(A,B\subseteq N\) with \(|A|=|B|=r\). Then
\begin{align}
\det Z[A,B]
&=\frac{1}{\tau_c(G)}
  \sum_{F\in\mathcal{F}_{r+1}}
  \chi_F(A)\chi_F(B)w(F).

\end{align}

