[Proposition lacunary-prop of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $\Pi$ be a fixed point of BBM with drift $\lambda \geq \sqrt{2}$ and let $\theta \in Dom_{\lambda}(\Pi)$ be a point process. Then, (recall Definition (def-lacunary of the paper))
 \begin{enumerate}
     \item For $\lambda > \sqrt{2}$, $\theta$ is lacunary.
     \item For $\lambda = \sqrt{2}$, $\theta$ is exponentially-lacunary. 
 \end{enumerate}

