[Lemma 60 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta} and \ref{Assumptions_basic} hold. Then there exists
$C>0$ depending only on the constants in the assumptions, such that for any $t >0$ and $\N$ large enough
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
& \quad \P\Bigg[\exists f\in \mathscr{H}_{\textnormal{Lip},\frac{1}{2}}\quad \Big|\quad \min_{h \in [H]} \bigg|\int_{\amsmathbb R} f(x) \dd(\mu_{\N,h} - \mu_h)(x)\bigg| \geq t |\!| f |\!|_{\frac{1}{2}}+ \frac{C}{\N}\big( |\!|f|\!|_\textnormal{Lip} +|\!|f|\!|_\infty \big)\Bigg] \\
& \leq \exp\bigg(C \N\log \N- \frac{t^2\N^2}{C}\bigg).
\end{split}
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

