[Lem lowerBound:expectation of arXiv:2607.09841, 'Mixing and cutoff for the systematic scan dynamics of the mean-field ferromagnetic Potts m'] For all integer $t \in \{0, \dots, n\sqrt n\}$, there exists constants $\rho = \rho(\beta, q)$ and $C = C(\rho, \beta,q)$ such that for any $\sigma_0 \in \Sigma_n^{\rho} \cap \tilde\Sigma_n^{\rho/2}$, we have
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb{E}\big[\lVert \alpha(\sigma_t) - \hat e \rVert _2^2\big] \geq C\gamma_n^{2t} - \frac{C}{n}.
\end{align*}

