body:
[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2605.11279, 'Flocking with Multiple Types: Competition, Fluid Limits and Traveling Waves'] Suppose $Z\sim \expo(1)$ and $v_-=0$. For each $t\in\real^+$, let $G_\pm(t) := H_\pm(-t)$. A traveling wave $H = \parens*{H_+, H_-}$ with mass partition $(\rho^+,\rho^-)$ and speed $\gamma$ is characterized by the following system of first-order ODEs:
    \begin{align}

        {\setlength{\nulldelimiterspace}{0pt}
        \left\{
        \begin{aligned}
            &G'_+ = -\dfrac{\rho^-}{\gamma} G_+ G_- - \dfrac{v_+ - \gamma + \alpha^+ - \rho^-}{\gamma} G_+ + \rho^-  \dfrac{(\rho^+ +\alpha^- + \gamma)}{\gamma \rho^+}G_- \\
            &G'_- = \dfrac{\rho^+}{\gamma} G_+ G_- - \dfrac{\rho^+ + \alpha^-}{\gamma} G_- + \rho^+  \dfrac{(\alpha^+ - \rho^-)}{\gamma \rho^-}G_+
        \end{aligned}
        \right.}.
    \end{align}

