[Lemma thm:upper_bound of arXiv:2509.16694, 'A central limit theorem for two-dimensional directed polymers with critical spatial correl'] Let $0\leq \zeta <\xi\le 1$ and recall (equation eq:Al of the paper). Then, for all $\hat \beta \in [0,z_a)$:
\begin{equation}

\limsup_{\delta\to 0}\, \limsup_{N\to\infty}\sup_{x_0\in [N^{\zeta - \delta},N^{\zeta+\delta}]\cap \mathbb{Z}^2_{even}} \Phi_{N^\xi}(x_0)\leq \frac{\tilde J_{\alpha}\Big( \hat{\beta}\zeta^{\frac{a+2}{2}}\Big)}{\tilde J_{\alpha}\Big( \hat{\beta}\xi^{\frac{a+2}{2}}\Big)}.
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
   \sup_{N\geq 1} \sup_{x_0\in\mathbb{Z}^2} \,\Phi_{N}(x_0) <\infty\,.
\end{equation}

