body:
[Lemma lem:g-bound of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] For the transition density $g_\rho(t,x)$ of a $1$-dimensional $\rho$-stable process, we have the following uniform upper and lower bounds:
\begin{equation}
\frac{C_1t}{\left(t^{\frac{1}{\rho}}+|x|\right)^{1+\rho}}\le g_\rho(t,x) \le \frac{C_2t}{\left(t^{\frac{1}{\rho}}+|x|\right)^{1+\rho}}\leq C_2t^{-\frac{1}{\rho}},\quad\forall~x\in\mathbb R~\text{and}~t>0,
\end{equation}
where $C_1,C_2$ are positive constants depending only on $\rho$. Moreover, for $t\leq T$, the lower bound can be simplified by $g_\rho(t,x)\geq \frac{C_1t}{\left(T^{1/\rho}+|x|\right)^{1+\rho}}$.

