[Theorem thm2 of arXiv:2510.17257, 'Rigidity of One-Dimensional Point Processes via Optimal Transport'] One-dimensional non-singular Riesz gases $\{\mathsf{P}_{s,\beta}\}$ with homogeneity parameter $-2<s \leq -1$, at any inverse temperature $\beta>0$, are $L^2$-perturbed lattices, 
	\eq{\mathsf{Wass}_2(\mathsf{P}_{s,\beta},\mathsf{P}^\mathbb{Z})<+\infty.} 
	In particular, these non-singular Riesz gases are Hyperuniform of type I, meaning $\ens{\mathrm{Var}_{\mathsf{P}_{s,\beta}} N_I}_{I \text{ interval}}$ is bounded. They are also Number-Rigid and have a Cyclic-Factor. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

