[Lemma eq:MHn72 of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Let $v>0$ and $(s_1, \ell_1), (s_2, \ell_2)$ be two points such that $s_1<s_2$. Suppose the ellipses in ((eq:v_ellipses of the paper)) intersects at $(t(v), h(v))$. Then the area of the region $E^{s_1,v}_{\ell_1}\cup E^{s_2,v}_{\ell_2}$ is given by

\begin{align}
|E^{s_1,v}_{\ell_1}\cup E^{s_2,v}_{\ell_2}|&= \begin{cases}
    \frac{1}{2v}\left[\pi \ell_1^2+vh(v)(s_2-s_1)+F_1(h(v), \ell_1,\ell_2)\right], & \text{ if }s_1<s_2< t(v),\\
    \frac{1}{2v}\left[ \pi \ell_2^2+\pi \ell_1^2+vh(v)(s_2-s_1)-F_2(h(v), \ell_1, \ell_2)\right], &\text{ if } s_1< t(v)<s_2,\\
    \frac{1}{2v}\left[\pi \ell_2^2+vh(v)(s_2-s_1)-F_1(h(v), \ell_1,\ell_2)\right], & \text{ if } t(v)<s_1<s_2,\\
    \end{cases}

\end{align}

where $t(v), h(v)$ as in ((eq:tvhv of the paper)) and the functions $F_1, F_2$ are as in ((eq:Lambda1 of the paper)) and ((eq:Lambda2 of the paper)).

