{"artifact_digest":"sha256:30dcb2e28facd9be4f22907e33b4441a481ae3d1c0357713be21a4b625dfe765","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/30/30dcb2e28facd9be4f22907e33b4441a481ae3d1c0357713be21a4b625dfe765.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:bbdc1b64663647a9c1c1352725ae12cf80f8a082db6f33812248fee9ecfc3388","bundle_entry_key":"2608-03497-lemma-7-boundary-rooting","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_086","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_086.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-03497-lemma-7-boundary-rooting","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Write \(x=\Psi_0^{-r}(q)\) with \(q\in V_0\).  If \(q=O\), take the
identity.  Otherwise define
\begin{equation}
  A_{r,x}
    =\Psi_0^{-r}\mathscr R_{q,O}\Psi_0^r.

\end{equation}
When \(r=0\), the reflection \(\mathscr R_{q,O}\) preserves \(V_0\) by (NF3) and is
therefore an automorphism of the nearest-neighbor graph \(F_0\).  When
\(r\ge1\), (NF3) in Definition~\ref{def:nested_fractal} says that
\(\mathscr R_{q,O}\) permutes the level-\(r\) fractal cells and their
