body:
[Lemma Inequalities of arXiv:2508.09291, '1+O(1) asymptotics for loop percolation in five and higher dimensions'] Define an event $A$ as increasing if $\eta\in A$ satisfies $\eta+\zeta\in A$ for all $\zeta$. Then for increasing $A,B$, the \textnormal{(FKG-inequality)} holds:
    \begin{equation} \mathbb{P}\left(A\cap B\right)\ge \mathbb{P}\left(A\right)\mathbb{P}\left(B\right)\, .
    \end{equation}
    Furthermore, write $A\Box B$ if $A$ and $B$ are realized through a disjoint set of loops (not edges!). We then have for $A,B$ increasing that \textnormal{(BK-inequality)}
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}\left(A\Box B\right)\le \mathbb{P}\left(A\right)\mathbb{P}\left(B\right)\, .
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop_1 of arXiv:2603.26307, '\LARGE The incompressible Navier--Stokes--Fourier system with thermal noise'] For every $\delta,\epsilon\in(0,1)$, there exists a weak martingale solutions to  (equation Eq_approx of the paper) with initial data $(u_0,\psi_0)$, which satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}|u_{\delta,\epsilon}(t)|^2 +|\psi_{\delta,\epsilon}(t)|^2 \,\mathrm{d} x \,+\, \epsilon \int_0^t \int_{\mathbb{T}^3} 
		|\Delta u_{\delta,\epsilon}  |^2 +
		|\Delta\psi_{\delta,\epsilon} |^2\,\mathrm{d} x \,\mathrm{d} s
		\,\leq\, \frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}|u_0|^2 +|\psi_0|^2 \,\mathrm{d} x\,+\,\epsilon t,
	\end{equation}
	for all $ t\in [0,T]$, $\mathbb{P}$-almost surely.

