body:
[Lem malthus of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Consider the branching process $\BP_\theta$. Then 
    \begin{enumeratea}
        \item The Malthusian rate of growth of the branching process $\BP_\theta$ namely $\lambda(\theta) =1$. 
        \item The offspring distribution satisfies the $X\log{X}$ condition. In particular $e^{-t}\BP_\theta(t)\stackrel{a.s., \mathbb{L}^1}{\longrightarrow} W_\theta$ where $W_\theta >0$ on the event of survival of the branching process namely  $\left\{|\BP_\theta(\infty)| = \infty\right\}$. 
    \end{enumeratea}

