[Lem 29 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on $X$. Then the functional $F:L^\infty(X)\to \R$, $f\mapsto \log\left(\int_X\exp(f(x))\ \mu(dx)\right)$ is continuous, convex and for $\gamma\in P_\mu(X)\subset (L^\infty(X))'$ the Fenchel conjugate is of the form
  \begin{align*}
      F^\ast(\gamma)=\int_X\log\left(\frac{d\gamma}{d\mu}(x)\right)\ \gamma(dx).
  \end{align*}

