[Lem lemlwp1 of arXiv:2608.30777, 'Inhomogeneous nonlinear Schr\"odinger equation \\ in Fourier-Lebesgue and modulation space'] Let $\alpha \in (1,5-2b),\, 0<b\leq 1/4$ and $p_{0}$  be as follows 
     \begin{gather*}
2>p_{0}>\begin{cases}
\vspace{0.2cm}
\max \left( \frac{\alpha+1}{\alpha}, \frac{4\alpha}{9-4b} \right) &\text{if} \quad \alpha \in  (1,3) \\ 
\vspace{0.2cm}
\max \left( \frac{2(\alpha-1)}{\alpha}, \frac{2\alpha}{5-2b} \right) \quad  & \text{if} \quad \alpha\in [3,5-2b).
\end{cases}
    \end{gather*}
    Then
    \begin{align*}
   \inf_{(\gamma,\rho)\in \mathcal{A}}\| ~|x|^{-b}|u|^{\alpha-1}v\|_{L^{\gamma'}_{T}L^{\rho '}}
   &\lesssim \|u\|_{X(T)}^{\alpha-1}\|v\|_{X(T)}
   \left(
     T^{1-\frac{\alpha-1}{2p_{0}}-\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{1}{p_{0}}-\frac{1}{2}\right)} 
     + T^{1-\frac{\alpha-1}{2p_{0}}-\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{1}{p_{0}}-\frac{1}{2}\right)-\frac{1}{\nu}}
\right).
\end{align*}

