[Theorem thm-specrelent of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] If $P\in{\mathcal M }_1^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm s}})}}}({\mathcal L }\times{\mathcal S })$ satisfies $\langle P,\mathfrak N_U^{\ssup\ell}\rangle <\infty$ (with $U=[-\frac 12,\frac 12]^d$ the unit box), then the limit in (equation jointentropydef of the paper) exists in $[0,\infty]$, and it satisfies
\begin{equation}
J_{W_R}(\Pi_{W_R}(P))\leq  {\rm h}^{\ssup{{\mathcal L },{\mathcal S }}}(P),\qquad R\in\mathbb{N}.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, the map $P\mapsto {\rm h}^{\ssup{{\mathcal L },{\mathcal S }}}(P)$ is lower semi-continuous and convex, and it is also concave (i.e., even affine). Moreover, for  any sequence $(K_{R_N})_{N\in\mathbb{N}}$ of compact sets $K_{R_N}\subset{\mathcal T }_{W_{R_N}}$ such that $R_N\to\infty$ as $N\to\infty$, the restricted level set 
\begin{equation}
\bigcap_{N\in\mathbb{N}}\big\{P\in{\mathcal M }_1^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm s}})}}}({\mathcal L }\times{\mathcal S })\colon \partial\Pi_{W_{R_N}}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(P)\in K_{R_N}, {\rm h}^{\ssup{{\mathcal L },{\mathcal S }}}(P)\leq c, \langle P,\mathfrak N_U^{\ssup\ell}\rangle \leq c\big\}
\end{equation}
is compact for any $c\in\mathbb{R}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

