[Lemma lem:2 of arXiv:2602.00988, 'Wealth exchange under ceiling and flooring constraints: a modified Bennati–Dragulescu–Yako'] Let ${\bf p}(t) = \{p_n(t)\}_{n\geq 0}$ be a classical solution to the system of nonlinear ODEs (equation eq:law_limit of the paper)-(equation eq:two-classes of the paper) with ${\bf p}(0) \in V_\mu$, we have
\begin{equation}
\sup\limits_{t\geq 0} \sum\limits_{n\geq 0} K^n\,p_n(t) \leq \max\left\{\frac{K^{b+1}+K^a}{1-\mu/b},\sum_{n\geq 0} K^n\,p_n(0)\right\}
\end{equation}
for all $K > 1$, provided that $\sum_{n\geq 0} K^n\,p_n(0) < \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:localNumeratorComm of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] There exists $\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}=\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}(\mu,v,n)>0$ such that for every $0<\gamma\le\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}$ and every $\sigma\in\{\pm1\}$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{N\ge1}
{\mathbb{E}}_{\mu^{\otimes N}}
\Bigg[\exp\pa*{
\sigma\frac{\gamma}{4C_{\mathrm{sr},n}\|\nabla v\|_{L^\infty}^n}
N\mathsf A_n(v,X_N,\mu)
-\gamma N\mathsf{F}_N(X_N,\mu)}\Bigg]
\le e+L.
\end{align}

