[Theorem 81 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $ p  = p(n) = (1 + \epsilon)/n$ with $n^{-1/3} \ll \epsilon \ll n^{-s}$, for some $s > 0$. Denote by $\cT_p$ a realization of the unweighted ($\beta = 0$) UST on $\cC_1(p)$. Then there exists some constant $c =c(s)> 0$ such that
    \begin{equation} 
        \widehat{\P} \Big( \frac{1}{(\log n)^c} \sqrt{\epsilon n} \leq \diam(\cT_p) \leq \sqrt{\epsilon n} (\log n)^c \Big) \xrightarrow{n \rightarrow \infty} 1.
    \end{equation}

