Here $S$ is the set of other items whose ages are smaller than $t$; item
$i$ is in the cache precisely when $\card S\le C-1$.

Expand
\[
        \prod_{j\in S}(1-e^{-p_jt})
        =
        \sum_{A\subseteq S}(-1)^{\card A}e^{-p_A t}.
\]
For a term indexed by $A\subseteq S$, put $B=S\setminus A$.  The ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:f6260df3eef67984ff3d1d2291cba61a7bf2f83e5125100fc2f5bd6e7971915d","revision_digest":"sha256:73036b6149be78d178025dbc5283c7cf9a2533e3ef17060f9a68a70508e4ec4b","source_id":"arxiv:2605.26107","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

