[Lemma K of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] If the strongly local regular Dirichlet form $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ on $L^2(X,\mu)$ satisfies (eq:HKMain of the paper) then there are constants $K \geq 1$ and $\sigma > 1$ depending only on the constants associated to $\Psi$ in (equation eq:PsiRad of the paper), the constants in (eq:HKMain of the paper) and the doubling constant of $\mu$ in (equation eq:muDoubling of the paper) such that
    \begin{align*}
        h_{x_0,R_0}(x) & \geq 2K \Psi(R_0) \text{ for all } x \in B(x_0,\kappa R_0),\\
        h_{x_0,R_0}(x) & \leq K \Psi(R_0) \text{ for all } x \in X \setminus B(x_0,\sigma R_0).
    \end{align*}
    Here $\kappa$ is the constant in (eq:HKMain of the paper).

