[Prop 10 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $f$ be a smooth non-negative function with compact support on $\C$,
and not identically zero.
Then the power series
\begin{displaymath}
\sum_{n=1}^{+\infty} \dfrac{\alpha^{n}}{n!} \E[(:\Theta_{\zeta_M}^{n}:\,,f)^{2}]^{1/2}
\end{displaymath}
has zero radius of convergence.
Similarly, for ever $\eta>0$, the power series
\begin{displaymath}
\sum_{n=1}^{+\infty} \dfrac{\alpha^{n}}{n!} \E[\Vert:\Theta_{\zeta_M}^{n}:\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}]^{1/2}
\end{displaymath}
has zero radius of convergence.

