[Proposition prop:incrementIt of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For any $\varphi\in\mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R} )$, any $0\le s<t\le T$, the diffusive term defined in (equation eq:It of the paper) satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}\left[ \big( \mathcal{I}_t^N(\varphi ) - \mathcal{I}_s^N(\varphi )\big)^2\right] \le C_{18}N^{2a-4} (t-s)^2 \|\Delta\varphi\|_{L^2}^2
    \end{equation}
    for some constant $C_{18}=C_{18}(\kappa ,\rho ,\mathcal{E})>0$.

