[Corollary cor:local_subgraph_clt_norho of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Under the same assumption as in Corollary (cor:local_subgraph_clt of the paper),
for all $\varepsilon > 0$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{d}_\mathrm{Was}\mleft(\frac{\mathsf{N}_G^{v}(X) - \mathbb{E}[\mathsf{N}_G^v(X)]}{2 \mathsf{e} p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} \varsigma_n}, Z\mright)
    \lesssim n^{-\frac{1}{4}+\varepsilon} + \delta_n.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:S6V-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] For $t \ge 1$ and
$\zeta \in \mathbb{C} \setminus \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$, the Fredholm
determinant $\mathcal{L}_{t,x,m}(\zeta)
= \det(I + K_{t,x,m})$ satisfies
\begin{align}
&(1 - b_1)
\mathcal{L}_{t,x+1,m+1}
\mathcal{L}_{t-1,x,m}
- (1 - b_2)
\mathcal{L}_{t-1,x,m+1}
\mathcal{L}_{t,x+1,m} \notag\\
&\qquad+ (b_1 - b_2)
\mathcal{L}_{t,x,m+1}
\mathcal{L}_{t-1,x+1,m}
= 0.
\end{align}

