[Proposition prop:Xn of arXiv:2512.17736, 'Pathwise uniqueness by noise for singular stochastic PDEs'] Assume (H0 of the paper), (H1 of the paper),
(H2_0 of the paper), (H3_0 of the paper), (H6_0 of the paper), and let $x\in H$. Then, 
for every $T>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n \to \infty}\sup_{t\in [0,T]}\mathbb{E}
\|X_{n}(t)-X(t)\|_H=0\,.
\end{equation}

